  ('cvh-021-02', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 21, 2, 'LESSON IV.', '<table><tr><td rowspan="2">Basin (lit. face pan.)</td><td rowspan="2">面盆</td><td rowspan="2">min'' p''un</td><td>Bad (not good)</td><td>唔好</td><td>''m-ho''</td></tr><tr><td>Very well!</td><td>好咯</td><td>ho'' lok</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="2">Towel (lit. face napkin.)</td><td rowspan="2">面巾</td><td rowspan="2">min''-kän</td><td>Good</td><td>好</td><td>ho''</td></tr><tr><td>Put</td><td>放</td><td>fong''</td></tr><tr><td>He, she, it</td><td>佢</td><td>k''ü''</td><td>Go</td><td>去</td><td>hü''</td></tr><tr><td>We</td><td>我哋</td><td>ngo''-ti''</td><td>Here (this place)</td><td>呢處</td><td>ni-ch''ü'': ni-shu''</td></tr><tr><td>His</td><td>佢嘅</td><td>k''ü''-ke''</td><td>There (that ,, )</td><td>响處</td><td>ko''-ch''ü'': ko''-shu''</td></tr><tr><td>Come</td><td>嚟,來</td><td>lai, loi</td><td>Above, upon</td><td>上高</td><td>sheung-ko</td></tr><tr><td>Our, ours</td><td>我哋嘅</td><td>ngo''-ti''-ke''</td><td>Below, beneath</td><td>下底</td><td>ha''-tai''</td></tr><tr><td>My, mine</td><td>我,我嘅</td><td>ngo'', ngo''-ke</td><td>At or on (also</td><td>在</td><td>tsoi''</td></tr><tr><td>You</td><td>你,你嘅</td><td>ni'', ni''-ke''</td><td colspan="3">meauing to be at or on.)</td></tr></table>

The verb to be may often be omitted if tsoi 在 be used, unless it be desired to emphasize the fact of a thing being in a given situation.

Ch''ü 處 is sometimes used by itself to express here, more especially when it merely means in place.

Possessives are formed from nouns and personal pronouns by the addition of ke嘅, but in every-day speech no distinction is observed between the nominative and possessive; e.g. my plate, NGO CHEK TIP, 我隻碟. There is no distinction of gender.', '<table><tr><tdrowspan="2">Basin(lit.facepan.)</td><tdrowspan="2">面盆</td><tdrowspan="2">min''p''un</td><td>Bad(notgood)</td><td>唔好</td><td>''m-ho''</td></tr><tr><td>Verywell!</td><td>好咯</td><td>ho''lok</td></tr><tr><tdrowspan="2">Towel(lit.facenapkin.)</td><tdrowspan="2">面巾</td><tdrowspan="2">min''-kän</td><td>Good</td><td>好</td><td>ho''</td></tr><tr><td>Put</td><td>放</td><td>fong''</td></tr><tr><td>He,she,it</td><td>佢</td><td>k''ü''</td><td>Go</td><td>去</td><td>hü''</td></tr><tr><td>We</td><td>我哋</td><td>ngo''-ti''</td><td>Here(thisplace)</td><td>呢處</td><td>ni-ch''ü'':ni-shu''</td></tr><tr><td>His</td><td>佢嘅</td><td>k''ü''-ke''</td><td>There(that,,)</td><td>响處</td><td>ko''-ch''ü'':ko''-shu''</td></tr><tr><td>Come</td><td>嚟,來</td><td>lai,loi</td><td>Above,upon</td><td>上高</td><td>sheung-ko</td></tr><tr><td>Our,ours</td><td>我哋嘅</td><td>ngo''-ti''-ke''</td><td>Below,beneath</td><td>下底</td><td>ha''-tai''</td></tr><tr><td>My,mine</td><td>我,我嘅</td><td>ngo'',ngo''-ke</td><td>Atoron(also</td><td>在</td><td>tsoi''</td></tr><tr><td>You</td><td>你,你嘅</td><td>ni'',ni''-ke''</td><tdcolspan="3">meauingtobeatoron.)</td></tr></table>Theverbtobemayoftenbeomittediftsoi在beused,unlessitbedesiredtoemphasizethefactofathingbeinginagivensituation.Ch''ü處issometimesusedbyitselftoexpresshere,moreespeciallywhenitmerelymeansinplace.Possessivesareformedfromnounsandpersonalpronounsbytheadditionofke嘅,butinevery-dayspeechnodistinctionisobservedbetweenthenominativeandpossessive;e.g.myplate,NGOCHEKTIP,我隻碟.Thereisnodistinctionofgender.', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-022-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 22, 1, NULL, 'The plurals our, your, their, are formed by adding 啲 TI

The plurals of nouns are formed by altering the classifiers to 啲 TI: as NI KO YAN 呢個人, this man, becomes NI TI YAN, 呢啲人, these men.

The possessive form of pronouns is seldom used in practice. Thus, instead of NGO KE CHEK TIP 我嘅隻碟, NGO CHEK TIP, 我隻碟 is more usual.

Lok 咯 is frequently added at the end of sentences for the sake of euphony.

And, as a copulative for substantives, (rendered by KUNG 共 and KAP 及) is not of very frequent use, and will not be translated in the first few lessons.

1 My knife; your fork | 我張刀,你枝叉 | ngo cheung to, ni chi ch''a
2 His place; my wine | 佢隻碟,我嘅酒 | k''ü chek tip, ngo-ke tsan
3 A good basin; bad tea; good water | 好面盆;唔好茶;好水 | ho min-p''un; ''m ho ch''a; ho shui
4 Have you my good sugar? | 你有我嘅好白糖呀 | ni yau ngo ke ho pak-t''ong a?
5 No; I have not good sugar | 冇,我冇好白糖 | mo; ngo mo ho pak-t''ong
6 Come here; bring my towel | 來呢處,擰我面巾來 | lai ni ch''ü; ning ngo min-kan loi
7 Have you the basin (and) towel? | 你有面盆面巾冇 | ni yau min-p''un min-kan mo?
8 I have a wine-glass (and) tumbler | 我有酒杯水杯 | ngo yau tsan-pui shui-pui
9 Put the tea there | 放茶個處 | fong ch''a ko ch''ü
10 Go (and) bring me a large fork | 去擰枝大叉來我 | hü, ning chi tai ch''a loi ngo
11 Get (a) tea-cup, tea (and) sugar | 拈茶杯,拈茶,拈白糖來 | nim ch''a-pui, nim ch''a, nim pak-t''ong loi
12 Is that his? is it ours? | 响嘅係佢嘅咩 | ko-ti hai k''ü ke me?
13 It is mine; it is hers | 係我嘅,係佢嘅 | hai ngo ke, hai k''ü ke
14 It is above; it is below | 在上,在下低 | tsoi sheung; tsoi ha-tai
15 We (are) above; they (are) below | 我哋在上高,佢哋下低 | ngo-ti tsoi sheung-ko; k''ü-ti tsoi ha-tai
16 Those (are) yours | 呢啲你嘅 | ni ti ke
17 Yours (are) above; mine (are) below | 你嘅在上高,我嘅在下低 | ni ke tsoi sheung-ko, ngo ke tsoi ha-tai
18 Put the towel in the basin | 放面巾在面盆 | fong min-kan tsoi min-p''un
19 Go there; bring a large fork | 去個處擰枝大叉來 | hü ko ch''ü; ning chi tai ch''a loi
20 Is this a large spoon? | 呢隻係大羹咩 | ni chek hai tai kang me?', 'Thepluralsour,your,their,areformedbyadding啲TIThepluralsofnounsareformedbyalteringtheclassifiersto啲TI:asNIKOYAN呢個人,thisman,becomesNITIYAN,呢啲人,thesemen.Thepossessiveformofpronounsisseldomusedinpractice.Thus,insteadofNGOKECHEKTIP我嘅隻碟,NGOCHEKTIP,我隻碟ismoreusual.Lok咯isfrequentlyaddedattheendofsentencesforthesakeofeuphony.And,asacopulativeforsubstantives,(renderedbyKUNG共andKAP及)isnotofveryfrequentuse,andwillnotbetranslatedinthefirstfewlessons.1Myknife;yourfork|我張刀,你枝叉|ngocheungto,nichich''a2Hisplace;mywine|佢隻碟,我嘅酒|k''üchektip,ngo-ketsan3Agoodbasin;badtea;goodwater|好面盆;唔好茶;好水|homin-p''un;''mhoch''a;hoshui4Haveyoumygoodsugar?|你有我嘅好白糖呀|niyaungokehopak-t''onga?5No;Ihavenotgoodsugar|冇,我冇好白糖|mo;ngomohopak-t''ong6Comehere;bringmytowel|來呢處,擰我面巾來|lainich''ü;ningngomin-kanloi7Haveyouthebasin(and)towel?|你有面盆面巾冇|niyaumin-p''unmin-kanmo?8Ihaveawine-glass(and)tumbler|我有酒杯水杯|ngoyautsan-puishui-pui9Puttheteathere|放茶個處|fongch''akoch''ü10Go(and)bringmealargefork|去擰枝大叉來我|hü,ningchitaich''aloingo11Get(a)tea-cup,tea(and)sugar|拈茶杯,拈茶,拈白糖來|nimch''a-pui,nimch''a,nimpak-t''ongloi12Isthathis?isitours?|响嘅係佢嘅咩|ko-tihaik''ükeme?13Itismine;itishers|係我嘅,係佢嘅|haingoke,haik''üke14Itisabove;itisbelow|在上,在下低|tsoisheung;tsoiha-tai15We(are)above;they(are)below|我哋在上高,佢哋下低|ngo-titsoisheung-ko;k''ü-titsoiha-tai16Those(are)yours|呢啲你嘅|nitike17Yours(are)above;mine(are)below|你嘅在上高,我嘅在下低|niketsoisheung-ko,ngoketsoiha-tai18Putthetowelinthebasin|放面巾在面盆|fongmin-kantsoimin-p''un19Gothere;bringalargefork|去個處擰枝大叉來|hükoch''ü;ningchitaich''aloi20Isthisalargespoon?|呢隻係大羹咩|nichekhaitaikangme?', 'verified'),
