  ('cvh-024-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 24, 1, NULL, 'To bring, when used of any article taken between the finger and thumb is拈 nim.*

With certain words "upon" is expressed by MIN面; thus upon the table, upon the ship''s deck, are T''OI MIN,檯面, SHUN MIN船面.

The word used for stairs in down-stairs, up-stairs, is properly a story; stairs are KAI KUP 階級.

Where, when, who, and similar words do not usually require an interrogative particle (such as NI, MO, &c.,) but the rule is not invariable.

The word PIN 邊 literally denotes side or place, but in interrogative adverbs it answers to who, which, or what? as PIN ch''ü 邊處 what place (that is, where?)

1 Bring me a chair; two chairs 拈一張椅來我,兩張椅 nim yat cheung i loi ngo; leung cheung i

2 I have three plates, and four 我有三隻碟,四張 ngo yau sam chek tip, sze knives 刀 cheung to

3 Where is the good wine? 响啲好酒喺邊處 ko ti ho tsau hai pin ch''ü?

4 It is on the large table 喺大檯面 hai tai t''oi min -

5 I want one basin and two 我要一個面盆,兩

towels 條面巾 ngo iu yat ko min-p''un, leung

t''iu min-kān

6 There are no good spoons 冇好匙羹 mo ho shi-kang

7 Very well, bring five chairs 好喇, 拈五張椅來 ho le, nim ''ng cheung i loi

8 The chair is upon the table 响張椅在檯面 ko cheung i tsoi t''oi min

9 The ice is beneath the table 响啲雪在檯下低 ko ti süt tsoi t''oi ha tai

10 Where are those seven tea-cups? 响七隻茶杯喺邊處 ko ts''at chek ch''a-pui hai pin ch''ü?

11 They are upstairs 係樓上 hai lau-sheung

12 Those chairs are downstairs 响啲椅係下低 ko ti i hai ha tai

13 Bring seven forks and one plate 擰七枝叉, 一隻碟來 ning ts''at chi ch''a, yat chek tip lai

14 That ice is in the basin 响啲冰喺面盆裡頭 ko ti ping hai min p''un lui t''au

15 Where is our table?

我哋响張檯喺邊處 ngo ti ko cheung t''oi hai pin ch''ü?

16 Your good tumbler is here 你嘅好水杯喺呢處 ni ke ho shui-pui hai ni ch''ü

17 That bread is bad; is it yours? 响啲麵飽唔好嘅, ko ti min-pau ''m ho ke, hai ni係你嘅唔係 ke ''m hai?

18 It is not mine, it is his 唔係我嘅, 係佢嘅 ''m hai ngo ke, hai k''u ke

