  ('cvh-034-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 34, 1, NULL, 'The student will note that several words, when used in sentences, very frequently take the second instead of their proper tones; e.g. yan, a man, lan'', to break, tan'', an egg, etc., become yan'', lan'', tan'', etc.

For (on account of) may be expressed by KWO 過 as MAI KWO NGO, 買過我, buy for me. It is not however always expressed in Chinese; e.g. Tell the coolie to buy that table for me, is KIU KUN TIM MAI KO CHEUNG T''OI NGO 叫管店買個張檯我.

The future, both positive and interrogative, is formed by making use of SEUNG 想 think or intend. Thus will you or do you like to go? NI SEUNG HÜ ''M NI 你想去唔呢. Will you sell? NI SEUNG MAI ''M NI 你想賣唔呢.

Several words are used by the Cantonese to designate themselves and their country. The most common is that given above; others are CHUNG-KWOK YAN 中國人 (central-kingdom man) PUN-TI YAN 本地人 (native soil man) PUNTI is used amongst themselves in contradistinction to HAKKA and HOKLO, (vide Introduction.)

1 Mend the clothes 補衣服 po i fuk

2 I want to buy a watch 我要買個時辰鏢 ngo iu mai ko shi-shān-piu

3 Come quickly and brush my boots 快啲來,擦我對靴 fai ti loi ts''at ngo tui hö

4 Sell me your umbrella 你把遮賣過我拉 ni pa ché mai kwo ngo la

5 I want to buy a bell and a lamp 我要買一個鐘,一盞燈 ngo iu mai yat ko chung, yat chàn tāng

6 Are you making a book? 你係整一簿書唔係 ni hai ching yat po shü ''m hai?

7 I am mending clothes 我補衣服 ngo po i fuk

8 Don''t break the bottle 唔好整爛响個罇 ''m ho ching lan ko ko tsun

9 It is a Chinese bottle 係唐人罇 hai t''ong yan tsun

10 Is it a Chinese watch? 係唐人時辰鏢唔係 hai t''ong yan shi-shān-piu ''m hai?

11 No it is not, it is mine 唔係,係我嘅 ''m hai, hai ngo ke

12 Ring the bell 打鐘 ta chung

13 Send (lit. make somebody call) for the coolie 使人叫管店來 shai yan kiu kun-tim loi

14 Tell a Chinaman to mend this 叫個唐人補翻呢的 kiu ko t''ong yan po fan ni ti

15 Call the cook; tell him to come quickly 叫廚夫叫佢快啲黎 kiu ch''ü fu k''ui k''ui fai ti lai

16 Will you buy a stick? 你想買枝鞭干唔呢 ni seung mai chi pin-kon ''m ni?

17 Will you sell that cork-screw? 你想賣個的酒鑽唔呢 ni seung mai ko ti tsau-tsun ''m ni', 'Thestudentwillnotethatseveralwords,whenusedinsentences,veryfrequentlytakethesecondinsteadoftheirpropertones;e.g.yan,aman,lan'',tobreak,tan'',anegg,etc.,becomeyan'',lan'',tan'',etc.For(onaccountof)maybeexpressedbyKWO過asMAIKWONGO,買過我,buyforme.ItisnothoweveralwaysexpressedinChinese;e.g.Tellthecoolietobuythattableforme,isKIUKUNTIMMAIKOCHEUNGT''OINGO叫管店買個張檯我.Thefuture,bothpositiveandinterrogative,isformedbymakinguseofSEUNG想thinkorintend.Thuswillyouordoyouliketogo?NISEUNGHÜ''MNI你想去唔呢.Willyousell?NISEUNGMAI''MNI你想賣唔呢.SeveralwordsareusedbytheCantonesetodesignatethemselvesandtheircountry.Themostcommonisthatgivenabove;othersareCHUNG-KWOKYAN中國人(central-kingdomman)PUN-TIYAN本地人(nativesoilman)PUNTIisusedamongstthemselvesincontradistinctiontoHAKKAandHOKLO,(videIntroduction.)1Mendtheclothes補衣服poifuk2Iwanttobuyawatch我要買個時辰鏢ngoiumaikoshi-shān-piu3Comequicklyandbrushmyboots快啲來,擦我對靴faitiloits''atngotuihö4Sellmeyourumbrella你把遮賣過我拉nipachémaikwongola5Iwanttobuyabellandalamp我要買一個鐘,一盞燈ngoiumaiyatkochung,yatchàntāng6Areyoumakingabook?你係整一簿書唔係nihaichingyatposhü''mhai?7Iammendingclothes我補衣服ngopoifuk8Don''tbreakthebottle唔好整爛响個罇''mhochinglankokotsun9ItisaChinesebottle係唐人罇hait''ongyantsun10IsitaChinesewatch?係唐人時辰鏢唔係hait''ongyanshi-shān-piu''mhai?11Noitisnot,itismine唔係,係我嘅''mhai,haingoke12Ringthebell打鐘tachung13Send(lit.makesomebodycall)forthecoolie使人叫管店來shaiyankiukun-timloi14TellaChinamantomendthis叫個唐人補翻呢的kiukot''ongyanpofanniti15Callthecook;tellhimtocomequickly叫廚夫叫佢快啲黎kiuch''üfuk''uik''uifaitilai16Willyoubuyastick?你想買枝鞭干唔呢niseungmaichipin-kon''mni?17Willyousellthatcork-screw?你想賣個的酒鑽唔呢niseungmaikotitsau-tsun''mni', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-035-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 35, 1, NULL, '<table border="1"><tr><td>18 No, I will sell the bell</td><td>唔係,我想賣個鐘啫</td><td>m hai, ngo seung mai ko chung che</td></tr><tr><td>19 How many watches have you?</td><td>你有幾多個時辰鏢呢</td><td>ni yau ki to ko shi-shān-piu ni?</td></tr><tr><td>20 I have nineteen pairs of socks</td><td>我有十九對襪</td><td>ngo yau shap-kau tui mät</td></tr><tr><td>21 Where is the tailor?</td><td>裁縫佬喺邊處呢</td><td>ts&#x27;oi fung lo hai pin ch&#x27;ü ni?</td></tr><tr><td>22 He has gone away</td><td>佢扯咯</td><td>k&#x27;ü ch&#x27;o lok</td></tr><tr><td>23 Tell a needle-woman to come</td><td>叫個補衣服婆黎</td><td>kiu ko po-i-fuk-p&#x27;oh lai</td></tr><tr><td>24 She is tearing the coat</td><td>佢撕破响件衫</td><td>k&#x27;ü sze p&#x27;o ko kin sham</td></tr><tr><td>25 I want to mend the shoes</td><td>我要補翻响對鞋</td><td>ngo iu po-fan ko tui hai</td></tr><tr><td>26 Mend these shoes for me</td><td>補翻呢對鞋過我</td><td>po-fan ni tui hai kwo ngo</td></tr><tr><td>27 Do you want to break the stick?</td><td>你要整爛個枝鞭杆咩</td><td>ni iu ching-lan ko chi pin-kon me?</td></tr><tr><td>28 Make a coat for me</td><td>整一件衫過我</td><td>ching yat kin sham kwo ngo</td></tr><tr><td>29 Buy a candle for me</td><td>買枝蠟燭過我</td><td>mai chi lap-chuk kwo ngo</td></tr><tr><td>30 Are you a Chinaman?</td><td>你係唐人唔係</td><td>ni hai t&#x27;ong yan &#x27;m hai?</td></tr><tr><td>31 I am not a Chinaman; what are you?</td><td>我唔係唐人,你係邊處人呢</td><td>ngo &#x27;m hai t&#x27;ong yan; ni hai pin ch&#x27;ü yan ni?</td></tr><tr><td>32 I am a tailor</td><td>我做裁縫嘅</td><td>ngo tso ts&#x27;oi fung ke</td></tr></table>', '<tableborder="1"><tr><td>18No,Iwillsellthebell</td><td>唔係,我想賣個鐘啫</td><td>mhai,ngoseungmaikochungche</td></tr><tr><td>19Howmanywatcheshaveyou?</td><td>你有幾多個時辰鏢呢</td><td>niyaukitokoshi-shān-piuni?</td></tr><tr><td>20Ihavenineteenpairsofsocks</td><td>我有十九對襪</td><td>ngoyaushap-kautuimät</td></tr><tr><td>21Whereisthetailor?</td><td>裁縫佬喺邊處呢</td><td>ts&#x27;oifunglohaipinch&#x27;üni?</td></tr><tr><td>22Hehasgoneaway</td><td>佢扯咯</td><td>k&#x27;üch&#x27;olok</td></tr><tr><td>23Tellaneedle-womantocome</td><td>叫個補衣服婆黎</td><td>kiukopo-i-fuk-p&#x27;ohlai</td></tr><tr><td>24Sheistearingthecoat</td><td>佢撕破响件衫</td><td>k&#x27;üszep&#x27;okokinsham</td></tr><tr><td>25Iwanttomendtheshoes</td><td>我要補翻响對鞋</td><td>ngoiupo-fankotuihai</td></tr><tr><td>26Mendtheseshoesforme</td><td>補翻呢對鞋過我</td><td>po-fannituihaikwongo</td></tr><tr><td>27Doyouwanttobreakthestick?</td><td>你要整爛個枝鞭杆咩</td><td>niiuching-lankochipin-konme?</td></tr><tr><td>28Makeacoatforme</td><td>整一件衫過我</td><td>chingyatkinshamkwongo</td></tr><tr><td>29Buyacandleforme</td><td>買枝蠟燭過我</td><td>maichilap-chukkwongo</td></tr><tr><td>30AreyouaChinaman?</td><td>你係唐人唔係</td><td>nihait&#x27;ongyan&#x27;mhai?</td></tr><tr><td>31IamnotaChinaman;whatareyou?</td><td>我唔係唐人,你係邊處人呢</td><td>ngo&#x27;mhait&#x27;ongyan;nihaipinch&#x27;üyanni?</td></tr><tr><td>32Iamatailor</td><td>我做裁縫嘅</td><td>ngotsots&#x27;oifungke</td></tr></table>', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-035-02', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 35, 2, 'LESSON XI.', 'Visiting card 拜帖 p''ai t''ip White 白色 pak-shik

To pay a visit 探 t''àm Red 紅色 hung-shik

Good morning 早晨 tso'' shan Blue 藍色 lam-shik

Good bye 好行 ho'' hang Yellow 黃色 wong-shik

Spectacles 眼鏡 ngan'' keng'' A word 一句說話 yat kü'' shüt wa''

Waistcoat (lit. back heart) 背心 pui-säm Somebody, one 人,有人 yan, yau yan

Beef 牛肉 ngau-yuk Cannot mend 唔補得翻 ''m po'' tāk fan

Mutton 羊肉 yeung-yuk Buy a little for me 買啲過我 mai'' ti'' kwo ngo''', 'Visitingcard拜帖p''ait''ipWhite白色pak-shikTopayavisit探t''àmRed紅色hung-shikGoodmorning早晨tso''shanBlue藍色lam-shikGoodbye好行ho''hangYellow黃色wong-shikSpectacles眼鏡ngan''keng''Aword一句說話yatkü''shütwa''Waistcoat(lit.backheart)背心pui-sämSomebody,one人,有人yan,yauyanBeef牛肉ngau-yukCannotmend唔補得翻''mpo''tākfanMutton羊肉yeung-yukBuyalittleforme買啲過我mai''ti''kwongo''', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-036-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 36, 1, NULL, 'Pork 猪肉 chü-yuk I am going to; intend to 我想 ngo'' seung''

Veal 牛仔肉 ngau-tsai''-yuk

Soup 湯 t''ong Have you bought (it)? 你有買冇 ni'' yau mai'' mo?

Vegetables 菜 ts''oi'' I have torn (it) 我撕破嘵 ngo'' sze p''o'' hiu

Fruit 菓子 kwoh''-tsz''

Black 黑色 hak-shik

The word YAN 人 man, one, somebody is used somewhat like the German man or the English one; e.g. one says (man sagt) YAN WA 人話.

Good morning and good bye are in Chinese (as are similar phrases in most languages) idiomatic expressions to which custom has affixed their peculiar meaning. TSO SHAN 早晨 is literally early time, and HO HANG 好行 good walk.

1 I want to put on my coat and trowsers 我要着衫褲 ngo iu cheuk sham fu

2 Have you a visiting card? 你有個拜帖冇 ni yau ko pai-t''ip mo

3 I have a white visiting card 我有個白拜帖 ngo yau ko pak pai-t''ip

4 Are you going to pay a visit? 你想去探人咩 ni seung hü t''am yan me?

5 Yes; good bye 係,好行喳 hai; ho hang chai

6 Good morning; have you a watch to sell? 早晨,你有時辰鏢賣冇 tso shàn; ni yau shi-shān-piu mai mo?

7 I have no watch to sell 我冇時辰鏢賣 ngo mo shi-shān-piu mai

8 Where are my spectacles? 我對眼鏡在邊處呢 ngo tui ngan-keng tsoi pin ch''ü ni

9 (They are) on the black table 在黑色檯面 tsoi hak-shik t''oi min

10 Mend my white waistcoat 補我件白背心 po ngo kin pak pui-sam

11 Buy beef and mutton 買牛肉羊肉嚟 mai ngau-yuk, yeung-yuk lai

12 Write the characters for soup and veal 寫湯字牛仔肉字 se t''ong tsz, ngau-tsai yuk, tsz

13 Send for some red thread 使人拈紅線黎 shai yan nim hung sin lai

14 Don''t tear the yellow handkerchief 唔好撕爛個條黃手巾 ''m ho sze lan ko t''iu wong shau-kān

15 Have you a blue coat? 你有件藍衫冇 ni yau kin lam sham mo?

16 I have not a blue coat; I have black shoes 我有藍衫,有對黑鞋啫 ngo mo lam sham, yau tui hak hai che

17 Have you bought the bread? 你有買麵飽冇 ni yau mai min-pau mo?', 'Pork猪肉chü-yukIamgoingto;intendto我想ngo''seung''Veal牛仔肉ngau-tsai''-yukSoup湯t''ongHaveyoubought(it)?你有買冇ni''yaumai''mo?Vegetables菜ts''oi''Ihavetorn(it)我撕破嘵ngo''szep''o''hiuFruit菓子kwoh''-tsz''Black黑色hak-shikThewordYAN人man,one,somebodyisusedsomewhatliketheGermanmanortheEnglishone;e.g.onesays(mansagt)YANWA人話.GoodmorningandgoodbyeareinChinese(asaresimilarphrasesinmostlanguages)idiomaticexpressionstowhichcustomhasaffixedtheirpeculiarmeaning.TSOSHAN早晨isliterallyearlytime,andHOHANG好行goodwalk.1Iwanttoputonmycoatandtrowsers我要着衫褲ngoiucheukshamfu2Haveyouavisitingcard?你有個拜帖冇niyaukopai-t''ipmo3Ihaveawhitevisitingcard我有個白拜帖ngoyaukopakpai-t''ip4Areyougoingtopayavisit?你想去探人咩niseunghüt''amyanme?5Yes;goodbye係,好行喳hai;hohangchai6Goodmorning;haveyouawatchtosell?早晨,你有時辰鏢賣冇tsoshàn;niyaushi-shān-piumaimo?7Ihavenowatchtosell我冇時辰鏢賣ngomoshi-shān-piumai8Wherearemyspectacles?我對眼鏡在邊處呢ngotuingan-kengtsoipinch''üni9(Theyare)ontheblacktable在黑色檯面tsoihak-shikt''oimin10Mendmywhitewaistcoat補我件白背心pongokinpakpui-sam11Buybeefandmutton買牛肉羊肉嚟maingau-yuk,yeung-yuklai12Writethecharactersforsoupandveal寫湯字牛仔肉字set''ongtsz,ngau-tsaiyuk,tsz13Sendforsomeredthread使人拈紅線黎shaiyannimhungsinlai14Don''tteartheyellowhandkerchief唔好撕爛個條黃手巾''mhoszelankot''iuwongshau-kān15Haveyouabluecoat?你有件藍衫冇niyaukinlamshammo?16Ihavenotabluecoat;Ihaveblackshoes我有藍衫,有對黑鞋啫ngomolamsham,yautuihakhaiche17Haveyouboughtthebread?你有買麵飽冇niyaumaimin-paumo?', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-037-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 37, 1, NULL, '<table border="1"><tr><td>18 Very well; good bye, come soon</td><td>好咯,好行喇,早啲翻黎啵</td><td>ho lok: ho hang lu, tso ti fan lai po</td></tr><tr><td>19 Red visiting cards</td><td>紅拜帖</td><td>hung pai-t&#x27;ip</td></tr><tr><td>20 He has torn the red visiting card</td><td>佢撕爛嘵响個紅拜帖</td><td>k&#x27;ü sze lau hiu ko ko hung pai-t&#x27;ip</td></tr><tr><td>21 This is a bad waistcoat</td><td>呢件唔好嘅背心</td><td>ni kin &#x27;m ho ke pui-sām</td></tr><tr><td>22 He cannot mend the waistcoat</td><td>佢唔補得翻個件背心</td><td>k&#x27;ü &#x27;m po tak fan ko kin pui-sām</td></tr><tr><td>23 Buy me a pair of white socks</td><td>買對白襪過我</td><td>mai tui pak mät kwo ngo</td></tr><tr><td>24 Light a candle and then bring me a pen and ink</td><td>點蠟燭,然後拈筆拈墨水黎我</td><td>tim lap-chuk, in hau niin pāt, nim mäk-shui lai ngo</td></tr><tr><td>25 Where are you taking that umbrella to?</td><td>你拈個把遮去邊處呢</td><td>ni nim ko pa che hü pin ch&#x27;u ni?</td></tr><tr><td>26 I am taking it to the tailor&#x27;s</td><td>我拈去裁縫佬處</td><td>ngo nim hü ts&#x27;oi-fung lo ch&#x27;u</td></tr><tr><td>27 Do you like vegetables?</td><td>你中意菜唔中意</td><td>ni chung i ts&#x27;oi &#x27;m chung i?</td></tr><tr><td>28 No, I like veal</td><td>唔中意,我中意牛仔肉</td><td>&#x27;m chung i; ngo chung i ngau-tsai-yuk</td></tr><tr><td>29 Good bye, I am going to buy a penknife</td><td>好行啫,我去買張刀仔</td><td>ho hang che, ngo hü mai cheung to-tsai</td></tr><tr><td>30 Send somebody for a needle-woman to mend my handkerchief</td><td>使人去叫個補衫婆黎,補翻我條巾</td><td>shai yan hü kiu ko po-shām-p&#x27;oh lai, po-fan ngo t&#x27;iu shau-kān</td></tr></table>', '<tableborder="1"><tr><td>18Verywell;goodbye,comesoon</td><td>好咯,好行喇,早啲翻黎啵</td><td>holok:hohanglu,tsotifanlaipo</td></tr><tr><td>19Redvisitingcards</td><td>紅拜帖</td><td>hungpai-t&#x27;ip</td></tr><tr><td>20Hehastorntheredvisitingcard</td><td>佢撕爛嘵响個紅拜帖</td><td>k&#x27;üszelauhiukokohungpai-t&#x27;ip</td></tr><tr><td>21Thisisabadwaistcoat</td><td>呢件唔好嘅背心</td><td>nikin&#x27;mhokepui-sām</td></tr><tr><td>22Hecannotmendthewaistcoat</td><td>佢唔補得翻個件背心</td><td>k&#x27;ü&#x27;mpotakfankokinpui-sām</td></tr><tr><td>23Buymeapairofwhitesocks</td><td>買對白襪過我</td><td>maituipakmätkwongo</td></tr><tr><td>24Lightacandleandthenbringmeapenandink</td><td>點蠟燭,然後拈筆拈墨水黎我</td><td>timlap-chuk,inhauniinpāt,nimmäk-shuilaingo</td></tr><tr><td>25Whereareyoutakingthatumbrellato?</td><td>你拈個把遮去邊處呢</td><td>ninimkopachehüpinch&#x27;uni?</td></tr><tr><td>26Iamtakingittothetailor&#x27;s</td><td>我拈去裁縫佬處</td><td>ngonimhüts&#x27;oi-fungloch&#x27;u</td></tr><tr><td>27Doyoulikevegetables?</td><td>你中意菜唔中意</td><td>nichungits&#x27;oi&#x27;mchungi?</td></tr><tr><td>28No,Ilikeveal</td><td>唔中意,我中意牛仔肉</td><td>&#x27;mchungi;ngochungingau-tsai-yuk</td></tr><tr><td>29Goodbye,Iamgoingtobuyapenknife</td><td>好行啫,我去買張刀仔</td><td>hohangche,ngohümaicheungto-tsai</td></tr><tr><td>30Sendsomebodyforaneedle-womantomendmyhandkerchief</td><td>使人去叫個補衫婆黎,補翻我條巾</td><td>shaiyanhükiukopo-shām-p&#x27;ohlai,po-fanngot&#x27;iushau-kān</td></tr></table>', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-037-02', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 37, 2, 'LESSON XII.', 'Trees 倉樹 p''oh shü'' Together, with, and 共 kung

