  ('cvh-044-02', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 44, 2, 'CONJUGATION OF NON-COMPOUND VERBS.', 'The Chinese word expressing a verb undergoes no change or inflexion on account of mood or tense.

The nominative, when expressed, precedes it as in English. In order to express the time of action (i.e. the different shades of meaning dependent on what we term moods and tenses) other words are added, or the verb is so placed in the sentence that the context sufficiently shews the intention of the speaker. The following table shews the principal parts of the active verb:—

<table border="1"><tr><td>Infinitive</td><td>To walk</td><td>行</td><td>hang</td></tr><tr><td>Present</td><td>I walk</td><td>我行</td><td>ngo hang</td></tr><tr><td>Imperfect</td><td>I walked</td><td>我行過</td><td>ngo hang kwo</td></tr><tr><td>Perfect</td><td>I have walked</td><td>我已經行咯,我有行嘵</td><td>ngo i king hang lok; ngo yau hang hiu</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="2">Potential</td><td>I can walk</td><td>我行得</td><td>ngo hang tăk</td></tr><tr><td>I may or can walk</td><td>我噲行</td><td>ngo ui hang</td></tr><tr><td>Subjunctive</td><td>If I walk</td><td>我若係行</td><td>ngo yeuk hai hang</td></tr><tr><td>Future</td><td>I shall or will walk</td><td>我將來行</td><td>ngo tseung loi hang</td></tr><tr><td>''''</td><td>I will (have an intention to) walk</td><td>我想行</td><td>ngo seung hang</td></tr></table>

The Chinese call a verb UT TSZ 活字 i.e. the "living" or "active" character. Note that the accusative or accusative phrase frequently precedes the verb.

The intensive particle 啫 CHE is frequently found following a verb. It is not translated.

<table><tr><td>1 Have you tobacco to sell?</td><td>你有烟餅賣冇</td><td>ni yau in-peng mai mo?</td></tr><tr><td>2 No; I have tobacco to smoke</td><td>冇, 我有烟食啫</td><td>mo; ngo yau in shik che</td></tr><tr><td>3 Will you begin to smoke?</td><td>你起首食烟唔呢</td><td>ni hi shau shik in ''m ni</td></tr><tr><td>4 Is breakfast ready?</td><td>早餐便唔曾</td><td>tso ts''an pin ''m ts''ǎng</td></tr></table>', 'TheChinesewordexpressingaverbundergoesnochangeorinflexiononaccountofmoodortense.Thenominative,whenexpressed,precedesitasinEnglish.Inordertoexpressthetimeofaction(i.e.thedifferentshadesofmeaningdependentonwhatwetermmoodsandtenses)otherwordsareadded,ortheverbissoplacedinthesentencethatthecontextsufficientlyshewstheintentionofthespeaker.Thefollowingtableshewstheprincipalpartsoftheactiveverb:—<tableborder="1"><tr><td>Infinitive</td><td>Towalk</td><td>行</td><td>hang</td></tr><tr><td>Present</td><td>Iwalk</td><td>我行</td><td>ngohang</td></tr><tr><td>Imperfect</td><td>Iwalked</td><td>我行過</td><td>ngohangkwo</td></tr><tr><td>Perfect</td><td>Ihavewalked</td><td>我已經行咯,我有行嘵</td><td>ngoikinghanglok;ngoyauhanghiu</td></tr><tr><tdrowspan="2">Potential</td><td>Icanwalk</td><td>我行得</td><td>ngohangtăk</td></tr><tr><td>Imayorcanwalk</td><td>我噲行</td><td>ngouihang</td></tr><tr><td>Subjunctive</td><td>IfIwalk</td><td>我若係行</td><td>ngoyeukhaihang</td></tr><tr><td>Future</td><td>Ishallorwillwalk</td><td>我將來行</td><td>ngotseungloihang</td></tr><tr><td>''''</td><td>Iwill(haveanintentionto)walk</td><td>我想行</td><td>ngoseunghang</td></tr></table>TheChinesecallaverbUTTSZ活字i.e.the"living"or"active"character.Notethattheaccusativeoraccusativephrasefrequentlyprecedestheverb.Theintensiveparticle啫CHEisfrequentlyfoundfollowingaverb.Itisnottranslated.<table><tr><td>1Haveyoutobaccotosell?</td><td>你有烟餅賣冇</td><td>niyauin-pengmaimo?</td></tr><tr><td>2No;Ihavetobaccotosmoke</td><td>冇,我有烟食啫</td><td>mo;ngoyauinshikche</td></tr><tr><td>3Willyoubegintosmoke?</td><td>你起首食烟唔呢</td><td>nihishaushikin''mni</td></tr><tr><td>4Isbreakfastready?</td><td>早餐便唔曾</td><td>tsots''anpin''mts''ǎng</td></tr></table>', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-045-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 45, 1, NULL, '5 Blow out the candle 吹息蠟燭 ch''ui sik lap-chuk

6 Bring me your bill 拈你張單來我 nim ni cheung-tan loi ngo

7 Alter this bill 改呢張單 koi ni cheung tan

8 I will not alter this bill 我唔想改呢張單 ngo ''m seung koi ni cheung-tan

9 Add up the account 計數目 kai sho muk

10 Burn it all 燒嘥 shiu sai

11 I wish to alter the bill 我想改响張單 ngo seung koi ko cheung-tan

12 Buy me some cigars 買的呂宋烟過我 mai ti Lü-Sung in kwo ngo

13 Will you sell me some oranges? 你想賣的柑我唔呢 ni seung mai ti kam ngo ''m ni?

14 I have bought some lychees 我買得啲荔枝咯 ngo mai tak ti lai-chi lok

15 Have you bought any flowers? 你買嘵花未 ni mai hiu fa me?

16 Clean the saucepan 整乾淨响個鑊 ching kon-tseng ko ko wok

17 Please change this for me 請找呢的過我 ts''ing chau ni ti kwo ngo

18 Will you copy characters? 你想抄字唔想 ni seung ch''au tsz ''m seung?

19 He may die 或者佢會死 wak che k''ü ui sze

