  ('cvh-051-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 51, 1, 'LESSON XVIII.', '<table><thead><tr><th>To repair</th><th>修整</th><th>sau ching''</th><td>City (walled)</td><td>城</td><td>shing</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>To row (with oars)</td><td>棹槳</td><td>chau` tseung''</td><td>Foreign</td><td>外國</td><td>ngoi kwok</td></tr><tr><td>To shave</td><td>剃</td><td>t''ai''</td><td>To return</td><td>翻來</td><td>fan loi</td></tr><tr><td>To sign (one''s name)</td><td>簽名</td><td>ts''im meug</td><td>To look for</td><td>揾</td><td>wăn''</td></tr><tr><td>Mountain</td><td>山</td><td>shan</td><td>To say or speak</td><td>話</td><td>wa''</td></tr><tr><td>Music</td><td>音樂</td><td>yǔm ngok</td><td>To separate</td><td>別開</td><td>pit-hoi</td></tr><tr><td>To ride</td><td>騎馬</td><td>k''e ma''</td><td>To shew</td><td>俾一睇</td><td>pi''—t''ai''</td></tr><tr><td>To sail (a ship)</td><td>駛船</td><td>shaí'' shün</td><td>Matches (lucifers)</td><td>火柴</td><td>foh''-ch''ai</td></tr><tr><td>To send</td><td>寄一去</td><td>ki''—hü''</td><td>People</td><td>百姓</td><td>pak-sing''</td></tr><tr><td>To sew</td><td>聯</td><td>lün</td><td>Native</td><td>本地</td><td>pun''-ti''</td></tr><tr><td>Weather</td><td>天氣</td><td>t''in-hi''</td><td>To tell</td><td>話一知</td><td>wa''—chi</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>A boat</td><td>三板</td><td>sam-pan''</td></tr></tbody></table>

The following characters are used to express the perfect tense: TS''ANG 曾 "have" "done," HIU 嘵 "have," LIU 了 "have," I 已 "just" done and I KING 已經 already; KWO 過 past action, "beyond." LOK 咯, LA 喇, LO 羅 and PA LO 罷囉 also express the perfect when used affirmatively or responsively; e.g., I have left NGO HÜ LIU 我去了; I have walked, NGO HANG KWO 我行過; I have copied it, NGO CH''AU LOK 我抄咯; He has died, k''ü SZ HIU 佢死嘵.

As will have been seen, the demonstrative pronoun frequently supplies the place of the definite article. It is generally so used when the sense admits of it, but the rule is by no means invariable.

1 Have you repaired the box?

你脩整好個个箱未曾

ni sau ching ho ko-ko seung mi ts''ang ?

2 Did you row the boat?

你棹嘵三板唔呢

ni chau hiu sam-pan ''m ni ?

3 I have seen many men

我見過好多人

ngo kin kwo ho to yan

4 Tell the man to shave me

呌响個人同我剃面

kiu ko-ko yan t''ung ngo t''ai min

5 Make him sign his name

强佢簽名

k''eung k''ü ts''im meng

6 Can you see the mountain?

你睇得見响個山唔得

ni t''ai tük kin ko-ko shan ''m täk ?

7 I want to go to my parents

我要去父母處

ngo iu hü fu mo ch''ü', '<table><thead><tr><th>Torepair</th><th>修整</th><th>sauching''</th><td>City(walled)</td><td>城</td><td>shing</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Torow(withoars)</td><td>棹槳</td><td>chau`tseung''</td><td>Foreign</td><td>外國</td><td>ngoikwok</td></tr><tr><td>Toshave</td><td>剃</td><td>t''ai''</td><td>Toreturn</td><td>翻來</td><td>fanloi</td></tr><tr><td>Tosign(one''sname)</td><td>簽名</td><td>ts''immeug</td><td>Tolookfor</td><td>揾</td><td>wăn''</td></tr><tr><td>Mountain</td><td>山</td><td>shan</td><td>Tosayorspeak</td><td>話</td><td>wa''</td></tr><tr><td>Music</td><td>音樂</td><td>yǔmngok</td><td>Toseparate</td><td>別開</td><td>pit-hoi</td></tr><tr><td>Toride</td><td>騎馬</td><td>k''ema''</td><td>Toshew</td><td>俾一睇</td><td>pi''—t''ai''</td></tr><tr><td>Tosail(aship)</td><td>駛船</td><td>shaí''shün</td><td>Matches(lucifers)</td><td>火柴</td><td>foh''-ch''ai</td></tr><tr><td>Tosend</td><td>寄一去</td><td>ki''—hü''</td><td>People</td><td>百姓</td><td>pak-sing''</td></tr><tr><td>Tosew</td><td>聯</td><td>lün</td><td>Native</td><td>本地</td><td>pun''-ti''</td></tr><tr><td>Weather</td><td>天氣</td><td>t''in-hi''</td><td>Totell</td><td>話一知</td><td>wa''—chi</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>Aboat</td><td>三板</td><td>sam-pan''</td></tr></tbody></table>Thefollowingcharactersareusedtoexpresstheperfecttense:TS''ANG曾"have""done,"HIU嘵"have,"LIU了"have,"I已"just"doneandIKING已經already;KWO過pastaction,"beyond."LOK咯,LA喇,LO羅andPALO罷囉alsoexpresstheperfectwhenusedaffirmativelyorresponsively;e.g.,IhaveleftNGOHÜLIU我去了;Ihavewalked,NGOHANGKWO我行過;Ihavecopiedit,NGOCH''AULOK我抄咯;Hehasdied,k''üSZHIU佢死嘵.Aswillhavebeenseen,thedemonstrativepronounfrequentlysuppliestheplaceofthedefinitearticle.Itisgenerallysousedwhenthesenseadmitsofit,buttheruleisbynomeansinvariable.1Haveyourepairedthebox?你脩整好個个箱未曾nisauchinghoko-koseungmits''ang?2Didyourowtheboat?你棹嘵三板唔呢nichauhiusam-pan''mni?3Ihaveseenmanymen我見過好多人ngokinkwohotoyan4Tellthemantoshaveme呌响個人同我剃面kiuko-koyant''ungngot''aimin5Makehimsignhisname强佢簽名k''eungk''üts''i