15 No, I broke it open 唔係，我打開佢 ''m hai; ngo ta hoi k''u', 'Lazily懶惰lan-toIbegpardon唔該''mkoiTryitonce試一試shiyatshi,試吓shihaIamengaged我有事ngoyauszeAgoodplan好計hokaiThatisright噉着咯komcheuklokTohaveleisure得開takhanLastly收尾shaumiMorethan過頭,kwot''au,Stop!罷咯,palok,多過tokwo停止t''ingchiThereissome有的好yautihoDon''tspeak唔好講''mhokonggood(init)sofast咁快komfai1Willyoubreakthatopento-你係今日打開个nihaikau-yattahoiko-ti''mday?啲唔係hai?2Icannot;inthefirstplaceI唔得;第一件我唔''mtak;taiyatkinngo''mts''angamnotready曾齊備ts''aipi3Hemakesabedprettywell佢幾噲鋪牀k''ükiuip''och''ong4Doeshelightthelampregu-佢常時點燈咩k''usheungshitimtangme?larly?5Hedoesnotdaretouchthe佢唔噉摩個盞k''ü''mkommohkochanlamp燈tung6Didheleavethedooropen?佢係打開度門唔係k''uhaitahoitomun''mhai?7Supposehehad;didyoutell譬如佢係，你有呌p''iük''ühai,niyaukiuk''üimhimtoshutit?佢掩埋有呀maimoa?8Ibegyourpardon,giveit唔該你俾過我''mkoi,nipikwongotome9Whydoeshekillthatcock-佢爲乜野打死個roach?隻甴曱k''uwai-mat-yetaszekochekkat-tsat?10Idon''tknow;hekillsthem我唔知,佢常時打ngo''mchi;k''üsheungshitaregularly死佢szek''ü11Tellhimtomakeafireand呌佢打火爐，然後kiuk''ütafo-lo,inhauimmaiafterwardsshutthedoor掩埋門mun12Ofcourseheisnotready自必然佢唔齊備tsz-pit-ink''ü''mts''aipi13.Hedoesthingssoslowly佢做野咁慢嘅k''ütsoyekommanke14Didyouknockatthedoor?係你拍門唔係hainipakmun''mhai?15No,Ibrokeitopen唔係，我打開佢''mhai;ngotahoik''u', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-063-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 63, 1, NULL, '16 Did he let the book go? 佢放開手個部書麼 k''ü fong hoi shau ko po shü mo?

17 No, not for a long time 冇,佢好耐都冇放手 mo, k''ü ho noi to mo fong shau

18 The compradore is very weak 個買辦好軟弱嘅 ko mai-pan ho ün yeuk ko

19 He is a coolie 佢係做管店嘅啫 k''ü hai tso kun-tim ke che

20 Extinguish that candle directly 即刻熄個啲蠟燭 tsik hak sik ko ti lap-chuk

21 It''s only a candle 單係蠟燭 tan hai lap-chuk

22 Is it therefore to be thrown 因咁所以擗佢去係 yan kom shoh-i p''ek k''ü hü hai away? 唔係 ''m hai?

23 No, light it again 唔係，再點着佢 ''m hai; tsoi tim cheuk k''ü

24 Are you busy? have you lei- 你有事冇，得閒唔 ni yau sze mo? tāk han ''m ni?

sure? 呢

25 No, I am engaged; don''t speak 唔得閒, 我有事, 唔 ''m tāk han; ngo yau sze; ''m ho so fast 好講咁快 kong kom fai

26 I intend to go tomorrow 我想聽日去 ngo seung t''eng yat hü

27 That''s right; its a good plan 噉着咯真好計 kom cheuk lok; chan ho kai

28 Are there more than fifty of 佢哋係多過五十 k''ü ti hai to kwo ''ng shap them? 唔係 ''m hai?

29 I cannot say, I have not 唔知得真，我冇數 ''m chi tāk chān; ngo mo sho counted them 過佢 kwo k''ü

30 Try to count them, and tell me 你試數吓佢就話過 ni shi sho ha k''ü; tsau wa kwo

how many there are 我聽有幾多 ngo t''eng yau ki to

31 There are more than a hundred 多過一百咯 to kwo yat pak lok

32 Don''t let him leave the door 唔好俾佢打開度 ''m ho pi k''ü ta hoi to mun open 門

33 If he does I won''t let him 若係佢噉做，我唔 yeuk hai k''ü kom tso, ngo ''m off 放過佢 fong'' kwo k''ü

34 There is some good in him, 佢有的好處，但係 k''ü yau ti ho ch''ü ; tan hai ngo but I don''t like him 我唔中意佢 ''m chung i k''ü', '16Didheletthebookgo?佢放開手個部書麼k''üfonghoishaukoposhümo?17No,notforalongtime冇,佢好耐都冇放手mo,k''ühonoitomofongshau18Thecompradoreisveryweak個買辦好軟弱嘅komai-panhoünyeukko19Heisacoolie佢係做管店嘅啫k''ühaitsokun-timkeche20Extinguishthatcandledirectly即刻熄個啲蠟燭tsikhaksikkotilap-chuk21It''sonlyacandle單係蠟燭tanhailap-chuk22Isitthereforetobethrown因咁所以擗佢去係yankomshoh-ip''ekk''ühühaiaway?唔係''mhai?23No,lightitagain唔係，再點着佢''mhai;tsoitimcheukk''ü24Areyoubusy?haveyoulei-你有事冇，得閒唔niyauszemo?tākhan''mni?sure?呢25No,Iamengaged;don''tspeak唔得閒,我有事,唔''mtākhan;ngoyausze;''mhosofast好講咁快kongkomfai26Iintendtogotomorrow我想聽日去ngoseungt''engyathü27That''sright;itsagoodplan噉着咯真好計komcheuklok;chanhokai28Aretheremorethanfiftyof佢哋係多過五十k''ütihaitokwo''ngshapthem?唔係''mhai?29Icannotsay,Ihavenot唔知得真，我冇數''mchitākchān;ngomoshocountedthem過佢kwok''ü30Trytocountthem,andtellme你試數吓佢就話過nishishohak''ü;tsauwakwohowmanythereare我聽有幾多ngot''engyaukito31Therearemorethanahundred多過一百咯tokwoyatpaklok32Don''tlethimleavethedoor唔好俾佢打開度''mhopik''ütahoitomunopen門33IfhedoesIwon''tlethim若係佢噉做，我唔yeukhaik''ükomtso,ngo''moff放過佢fong''kwok''ü34Thereissomegoodinhim,佢有的好處，但係k''üyautihoch''ü;tanhaingobutIdon''tlikehim我唔中意佢''mchungik''ü', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-064-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 64, 1, 'LESSON XXIII.', 'To return 翻黎 fan lai A fragment, a bit 碎, 片 suì'' p''in''

What 乜野 mät-ye'' To live, reside 住 chü''

To know (be知到 chi-to'' Any longer (in耐的 noi'' ti aware of) time)

