Fire 火 foh''', 'Toreturn翻黎fanlaiAfragment,abit碎,片suì''p''in''What乜野mät-ye''Tolive,reside住chü''Toknow(be知到chi-to''Anylonger(in耐的noi''tiawareof)time)Toset(atable)櫅好chaiho''Exactly正正ching''-ching''Tobetired癐,倦kui'',kun''Notquite爭啲changtiWith同t''ungName(givenaf-名mingTosave(putby)剩翻shing''fanterbirth)Towaste多費tofai''Tobeinan替,打工,t''ai,ta''kung,Expensive(dear)貴kwai''employ有工打yau''kungta''Fire火foh''', 'needs_review'),
  ('cvh-064-02', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 64, 2, 'PARTICLES.', 'The vernaculars of Chinese abound in untranslatable particles, of which the student will come across several examples in this and following exercises. They are never found at the beginning of a phrase, but seldom in the middle of it, and generally at the end. They are called by the people LI YAM 唎音 or "tongue sounds" and probably owe their origin to the difficulties experienced by Chinese in checking their utterance of certain final sounds,—as exemplified in "pidgin" English in which like becomes likee, catch, eatchee, &c. They have now, however, acquired specific values as intensifying the affirmation, question, or doubt expressed by the sentences in which they occur.

The following are those most commonly used, the second character, where two are given, being more intensive than the first.

1. Imperative particle - la 喇 la'' □

2. Responsive particle in answering questions lok 咯 lo 囉

3. Interrogative particle - ni 呢 a 呀 a'' 亞

NI 呢, is occasionally used as responsive.

1 Tell him to return 呌佢翻黎喇 kiu k''ü fan lai la

2 He says be is tired 佢話癐咯 k''ü wa kui lok

3. What has he been doing? 佢做過乜野嚟呢 k''ii tso-kwo màt-ye lai ni?

4 I really don''t know 我唔知得實咯 ngo ''m chi-tāk shat lok

5 He works very slowly 佢做工夫係好慢嘅 k''ü tso kung-fu hai ho man ke', 'ThevernacularsofChineseaboundinuntranslatableparticles,ofwhichthestudentwillcomeacrossseveralexamplesinthisandfollowingexercises.Theyareneverfoundatthebeginningofaphrase,butseldominthemiddleofit,andgenerallyattheend.TheyarecalledbythepeopleLIYAM唎音or"tonguesounds"andprobablyowetheirorigintothedifficultiesexperiencedbyChineseincheckingtheirutteranceofcertainfinalsounds,—asexemplifiedin"pidgin"Englishinwhichlikebecomeslikee,catch,eatchee,&c.Theyhavenow,however,acquiredspecificvaluesasintensifyingtheaffirmation,question,ordoubtexpressedbythesentencesinwhichtheyoccur.Thefollowingarethosemostcommonlyused,thesecondcharacter,wheretwoaregiven,beingmoreintensivethanthefirst.1.Imperativeparticle-la喇la''□2.Responsiveparticleinansweringquestionslok咯lo囉3.Interrogativeparticle-ni呢a呀a''亞NI呢,isoccasionallyusedasresponsive.1Tellhimtoreturn呌佢翻黎喇kiuk''üfanlaila2Hesaysbeistired佢話癐咯k''üwakuilok3.Whathashebeendoing?佢做過乜野嚟呢k''iitso-kwomàt-yelaini?4Ireallydon''tknow我唔知得實咯ngo''mchi-tākshatlok5Heworksveryslowly佢做工夫係好慢嘅k''ütsokung-fuhaihomanke', 'needs_review'),
  ('cvh-065-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 65, 1, NULL, '<table border="1"><tr><td>6 Does he know how to set a table?</td><td>佢噲櫅好檯啲野唔噲呢</td><td>k&#x27;ü ui chai-ho t&#x27;oi ti ye &#x27;m ui ni?</td></tr><tr><td>7 Yes, pretty well but not very well</td><td>噲咯，幾好，但唔係十分好啫</td><td>ui lok, ki ho; tan &#x27;m hai shap-fan ho che</td></tr><tr><td>8 Tell him to save that meat</td><td>呌佢剩翻个的肉</td><td>kiu k&#x27;ü shing-fan ko-ti yuk</td></tr><tr><td>9 He broke open the box</td><td>佢撬開嘵個个箱</td><td>k&#x27;ü kiu-hoi hiu ko-ko seung</td></tr><tr><td>10 Has he left the door open?</td><td>佢有打開個度門冇呀</td><td>k&#x27;ü yau ta hoi ko to-mun mo a?</td></tr><tr><td>11 No; he shut it at once</td><td>冇,佢卽刻閂埋喇</td><td>mo; k&#x27;ü tsik hak shan mai la</td></tr><tr><td>12 Will he waste that sugar?</td><td>佢想多費个的白糖唔呢</td><td>k&#x27;ü seung to-fai ko ti pak-t&#x27;ong &#x27;m ni?</td></tr><tr><td>13 No; it is too expensive</td><td>唔咯，貴過頭</td><td>&#x27;m lok; kwai kwo t&#x27;au</td></tr><tr><td>14 Where does he reside?</td><td>佢喺邊處住呢</td><td>k&#x27;ü hai pin-ch&#x27;ü chü ni?</td></tr><tr><td>15 He lives with me</td><td>佢同我住咯</td><td>k&#x27;ü t&#x27;ung ngo chü lok</td></tr><tr><td>16 Will he live with you any longer?</td><td>佢想同你住耐啲麼</td><td>k&#x27;ü seung t&#x27;ung ni chü noi ti mo?</td></tr><tr><td>17 He will live several years with me</td><td>佢想同我住數年</td><td>k&#x27;ü seung t&#x27;ung ngo chü sho nin</td></tr><tr><td>18 He has not been here quite a year</td><td>佢喺處爭啲一年</td><td>k&#x27;ü hai ch&#x27;ü chàng-ti yat nin</td></tr><tr><td>19 It is eleven months exactly</td><td>正正十一個月咯</td><td>ching-chíng shap yat ko üt lok</td></tr><tr><td>20 How long have they been in your employ?</td><td>佢哋喺你處做嘵幾耐呢</td><td>k&#x27;ü ti hai ni ch&#x27;ü tso hiu ki noi ni?</td></tr><tr><td>21 All last year and part of this</td><td>舊年成年；又今年幾個月</td><td>kau nin shing niu; yau kàm nin ki-ko üt</td></tr><tr><td>22 What is the name of that man?</td><td>個个人呌也名呢</td><td>ko ko yan kiu mät ming ni?</td></tr><tr><td>23 I don&#x27;t know, I think it is A-yau</td><td>我唔知，我估係亞有</td><td>ngo &#x27;m chi; ngo ku hai A-yau</td></tr><tr><td>24 I am very tired, I have been studying</td><td>我十分癐咯，我讀書嚟</td><td>ngo shap-fàn kui lok; ngo tuk shü lai</td></tr><tr><td>25 How long have you been studying?</td><td>你讀書幾耐呢</td><td>ni tuk shü ki noi ni?</td></tr><tr><td>26 Several hours; I study regularly</td><td>讀嘵幾點鐘啫，我時時讀咯</td><td>tuk hiu ki tim chung che; ngo shi-shi tuk lok</td></tr></table>', '<tableborder="1"><tr><td>6Doesheknowhowtosetatable?</td><td>佢噲櫅好檯啲野唔噲呢</td><td>k&#x27;üuichai-hot&#x27;oitiye&#x27;muini?</td></tr><tr><td>7Yes,prettywellbutnotverywell</td><td>噲咯，幾好，但唔係十分好啫</td><td>uilok,kiho;tan&#x27;mhaishap-fanhoche</td></tr><tr><td>8Tellhimtosavethatmeat</td><td>呌佢剩翻个的肉</td><td>kiuk&#x27;üshing-fanko-tiyuk</td></tr><tr><td>9Hebrokeopenthebox</td><td>佢撬開嘵個个箱</td><td>k&#x27;ükiu-hoihiuko-koseung</td></tr><tr><td>10Hasheleftthedooropen?</td><td>佢有打開個度門冇呀</td><td>k&#x27;üyautahoikoto-munmoa?</td></tr><tr><td>11No;heshutitatonce</td><td>冇,佢卽刻閂埋喇</td><td>mo;k&#x27;ütsikhakshanmaila</td></tr><tr><td>12Willhewastethatsugar?</td><td>佢想多費个的白糖唔呢</td><td>k&#x27;üseungto-faikotipak-t&#x27;ong&#x27;mni?</td></tr><tr><td>13No;itistooexpensive</td><td>唔咯，貴過頭</td><td>&#x27;mlok;kwaikwot&#x27;au</td></tr><tr><td>14Wheredoeshereside?</td><td>佢喺邊處住呢</td><td>k&#x27;ühaipin-ch&#x27;üchüni?</td></tr><tr><td>15Heliveswithme</td><td>佢同我住咯</td><td>k&#x27;üt&#x27;ungngochülok</td></tr><tr><td>16Willhelivewithyouanylonger?</td><td>佢想同你住耐啲麼</td><td>k&#x27;üseungt&#x27;ungnichünoitimo?</td></tr><tr><td>17Hewillliveseveralyearswithme</td><td>佢想同我住數年</td><td>k&#x27;üseungt&#x27;ungngochüshonin</td></tr><tr><td>18Hehasnotbeenherequiteayear</td><td>佢喺處爭啲一年</td><td>k&#x27;ühaich&#x27;üchàng-tiyatnin</td></tr><tr><td>19Itiselevenmonthsexactly</td><td>正正十一個月咯</td><td>ching-chíngshapyatkoütlok</td></tr><tr><td>20Howlonghavetheybeeninyouremploy?</td><td>佢哋喺你處做嘵幾耐呢</td><td>k&#x27;ütihainich&#x27;ütsohiukinoini?</td></tr><tr><td>21Alllastyearandpartofthis</td><td>舊年成年；又今年幾個月</td><td>kauninshingniu;yaukàmninki-koüt</td></tr><tr><td>22Whatisthenameofthatman?</td><td>個个人呌也名呢</td><td>kokoyankiumätmingni?</td></tr><tr><td>23Idon&#x27;tknow,IthinkitisA-yau</td><td>我唔知，我估係亞有</td><td>ngo&#x27;mchi;ngokuhaiA-yau</td></tr><tr><td>24Iamverytired,Ihavebeenstudying</td><td>我十分癐咯，我讀書嚟</td><td>ngoshap-fànkuilok;ngotukshülai</td></tr><tr><td>25Howlonghaveyoubeenstudying?</td><td>你讀書幾耐呢</td><td>nitukshükinoini?</td></tr><tr><td>26Severalhours;Istudyregularly</td><td>讀嘵幾點鐘啫，我時時讀咯</td><td>tukhiukitimchungche;ngoshi-shituklok</td></tr></table>', 'needs_review'),
  ('cvh-066-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 66, 1, NULL, '<table border="1"><tr><td>27 Have you a piece of bread here?</td><td>呢處有碎麵飽冇</td><td>ni ch&#x27;ü yau sui min-pau mo?</td></tr><tr><td>28 No, I have wine, coffee, and rice</td><td>冇咯,我有酒架啡同飯啫</td><td>mo lok! ngo yau tsau, ka-fe,t&#x27;ung fan che</td></tr><tr><td>29 Send that man away</td><td>呌個个人咀喇</td><td>kin ko-ko yan c&#x27;he la</td></tr><tr><td>30 Why does he not sweep the room?</td><td>佢也唔掃个間房呢</td><td>k&#x27;ü mät &#x27;m so ko kan fong ni?</td></tr><tr><td>31 He cannot sweep it quickly</td><td>佢唔掃得快啫</td><td>k&#x27;ü &#x27;m so-tāk fai che</td></tr><tr><td>32 Why not? He understands</td><td>也唔得呢,佢識得</td><td>mät &#x27;m tāk ni? k&#x27;ü shik tāk</td></tr><tr><td>33 No, he does not, I will teach him</td><td>佢唔識得,我教佢啫</td><td>k&#x27;ü &#x27;m shik tāk, ngo kau k&#x27;ü che</td></tr><tr><td>34 He must not remain any longer</td><td>佢唔好等耐啲添咯</td><td>k&#x27;ü &#x27;m ho tāng noi ti t&#x27;im lok</td></tr><tr><td>35 Good bye, I am going out*</td><td>坐喳,我出去咯</td><td>tso cha! ngo ch&#x27;ut hü lok</td></tr><tr><td>36 If you are going out buy me a pen</td><td>你若係出去買枝筆過我喇</td><td>ni yeuk hai ch&#x27;ut hü, mài chi pat kwo ngo la</td></tr></table>', '<tableborder="1"><tr><td>27Haveyouapieceofbreadhere?</td><td>呢處有碎麵飽冇</td><td>nich&#x27;üyausuimin-paumo?</td></tr><tr><td>28No,Ihavewine,coffee,andrice</td><td>冇咯,我有酒架啡同飯啫</td><td>molok!ngoyautsau,ka-fe,t&#x27;ungfanche</td></tr><tr><td>29Sendthatmanaway</td><td>呌個个人咀喇</td><td>kinko-koyanc&#x27;hela</td></tr><tr><td>30Whydoeshenotsweeptheroom?</td><td>佢也唔掃个間房呢</td><td>k&#x27;ümät&#x27;msokokanfongni?</td></tr><tr><td>31Hecannotsweepitquickly</td><td>佢唔掃得快啫</td><td>k&#x27;ü&#x27;mso-tākfaiche</td></tr><tr><td>32Whynot?Heunderstands</td><td>也唔得呢,佢識得</td><td>mät&#x27;mtākni?k&#x27;üshiktāk</td></tr><tr><td>33No,hedoesnot,Iwillteachhim</td><td>佢唔識得,我教佢啫</td><td>k&#x27;ü&#x27;mshiktāk,ngokauk&#x27;üche</td></tr><tr><td>34Hemustnotremainanylonger</td><td>佢唔好等耐啲添咯</td><td>k&#x27;ü&#x27;mhotāngnoitit&#x27;imlok</td></tr><tr><td>35Goodbye,Iamgoingout*</td><td>坐喳,我出去咯</td><td>tsocha!ngoch&#x27;uthülok</td></tr><tr><td>36Ifyouaregoingoutbuymeapen</td><td>你若係出去買枝筆過我喇</td><td>niyeukhaich&#x27;uthü,màichipatkwongola</td></tr></table>', 'needs_review'),
  ('cvh-066-02', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 66, 2, 'LESSON XXIV.', 'A very large number of verbs used in the Chinese vernaculars are compound, their invariable use in this way indeed, by itself justifying the assertion, already made, that the spoken vernaculars are not monosyllabic. The words with which they are most frequently compounded are as follows.

<table border="1"><tr><td>K&#x27;euk</td><td>却</td><td>to stop(a causative particle)</td><td>Mai</td><td>埋</td><td>to conceal, connect with</td></tr><tr><td>Chii&#x27;</td><td>住</td><td>to dwell</td><td>Ch&#x27;ut</td><td>出</td><td>to go out</td></tr><tr><td>Hi&#x27;</td><td>起</td><td>to rise</td><td>Hii&#x27;</td><td>去</td><td>to go</td></tr><tr><td>To&#x27;</td><td>到</td><td>to arrive at</td><td>Loi</td><td>來</td><td>to come</td></tr><tr><td>Tu&#x27;</td><td>倒</td><td>to fall down</td><td>Tu&#x27;</td><td>打</td><td>to strike</td></tr></table>

And a few others. Of all of these numerous examples will occur in future lessons.

