PARTICLES (CONTINUED.)

4. Affirmative particles Li 哩 Le'' 咧

5. Interrogative and Responsive particle often conveying an idea of disapprobation Me 咩

6. Restrictive particles often used in answers but seldom in questions Che 啫 Chi'' 啡

7. Doubting particle expressing doubt Kwa'' 啩

8. Desiderating particle expressing desire Ai 唉

9. Admonishing or directing particles, not so intense as to convey the idea of command Po'' 噃 O 呵

In some cases two of these are conjoined: thus LO'' PO'' (Nos. 2. & 9 ) have the force of a strongly declarative expression.

