  ('cvh-072-02', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 72, 2, 'LESSON XXVI.', 'To be careful (lit. 小心 sin'' sām People (all men) 人人 yan yan

little heart)

Weak (as a decoction)淡 tam`

Do. 好嚷 ho'' sheng

Strong (do.)濃 yung

To wait 等 tang''

Strong (as an essence) 強 k''ang''

Wait a little 等吓 tōng'' ha''

Strong (in muscle) 有力 yau'' lik

Daily (all days) 日日 yat yat

Number, like gender, is in Chinese only expressed when distinctness is required, the same word being ordinarily used to signify either singular or plural. To form specific plurals the noun is, in some few cases, repeated as above; in other cases TANG 等 and TI 哋 are suffixed.

Men 人哋 yan ti`

Us 我等, 我哋 ngo''-tung'', ngo''-ti`

You 你等, 你哋 ni''-tung'', ni''-ti`

Note that the noun very seldom has a plural suffix, even when it is desired to speak of more than one object, if a demonstrative pronoun in the plural form precedes it.

Those tables 個啲檯 ko'' ti t''oi

These plates 呢啲碟 ni'' ti tip

The classifier is less often used with a plural pronoun than when the singular form only is used.', 'Tobecareful(lit.小心sin''sāmPeople(allmen)人人yanyanlittleheart)Weak(asadecoction)淡tam`Do.好嚷ho''shengStrong(do.)濃yungTowait等tang''Strong(asanessence)強k''ang''Waitalittle等吓tōng''ha''Strong(inmuscle)有力yau''likDaily(alldays)日日yatyatNumber,likegender,isinChineseonlyexpressedwhendistinctnessisrequired,thesamewordbeingordinarilyusedtosignifyeithersingularorplural.Toformspecificpluralsthenounis,insomefewcases,repeatedasabove;inothercasesTANG等andTI哋aresuffixed.Men人哋yanti`Us我等,我哋ngo''-tung'',ngo''-ti`You你等,你哋ni''-tung'',ni''-ti`Notethatthenounveryseldomhasapluralsuffix,evenwhenitisdesiredtospeakofmorethanoneobject,ifademonstrativepronouninthepluralformprecedesit.Thosetables個啲檯ko''tit''oiTheseplates呢啲碟ni''titipTheclassifierislessoftenusedwithapluralpronounthanwhenthesingularformonlyisused.', 'needs_review'),
