  ('cvh-079-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 79, 1, NULL, '<table border="1"><tr><td>36 It is a house; it stands (lit. is erected) by the side of the bridge</td><td>係屋嚟, 建在响度橋邊嘅呢</td><td>hai uk lai; kin tsoi ko to k''iu pin ke ni</td></tr><tr><td>37 I want some men to translate for me</td><td>我要人同我譒繹</td><td>ngo iu yan t''ung ngo fan-yik</td></tr><tr><td>38 They must not be English but Chinese</td><td>唔係要英人,要唐人啫</td><td>''m hai iu ying-yan; in t''ong-yan che</td></tr><tr><td>39 Tell her I don''t want him any longer</td><td>話佢知,我唔要佢耐啲添喇</td><td>wa k''ü chi; ngo ''m iu k''ü noi ti t''im la</td></tr><tr><td>40 He comes here very regularly</td><td>佢常常喺呢邊來</td><td>k''ü sheung-sheung hai ni-pin loi</td></tr><tr><td>41 Of course he does; he is a friend</td><td>自必然係喇,佢係朋友啫</td><td>tze-pit-in hai la; k''ü hai p''ǎng-yan che</td></tr><tr><td>42 When he comes I wish to have some conversation with him</td><td>佢嚟時,我想同佢講吓說話</td><td>k''ü lai shi, ngo seung t''ung k''ü kong ha shüt wa</td></tr></table>', '<tableborder="1"><tr><td>36Itisahouse;itstands(lit.iserected)bythesideofthebridge</td><td>係屋嚟,建在响度橋邊嘅呢</td><td>haiuklai;kintsoikotok''iupinkeni</td></tr><tr><td>37Iwantsomementotranslateforme</td><td>我要人同我譒繹</td><td>ngoiuyant''ungngofan-yik</td></tr><tr><td>38TheymustnotbeEnglishbutChinese</td><td>唔係要英人,要唐人啫</td><td>''mhaiiuying-yan;int''ong-yanche</td></tr><tr><td>39TellherIdon''twanthimanylonger</td><td>話佢知,我唔要佢耐啲添喇</td><td>wak''üchi;ngo''miuk''ünoitit''imla</td></tr><tr><td>40Hecomeshereveryregularly</td><td>佢常常喺呢邊來</td><td>k''üsheung-sheunghaini-pinloi</td></tr><tr><td>41Ofcoursehedoes;heisafriend</td><td>自必然係喇,佢係朋友啫</td><td>tze-pit-inhaila;k''ühaip''ǎng-yanche</td></tr><tr><td>42WhenhecomesIwishtohavesomeconversationwithhim</td><td>佢嚟時,我想同佢講吓說話</td><td>k''ülaishi,ngoseungt''ungk''ükonghashütwa</td></tr></table>', 'verified'),
