  ('cvh-086-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 86, 1, NULL, '<table border="1"><tr><td>23 I forget what they do there</td><td>我唔記得佢哋在响處做乜野</td><td>ngo ''m ki-tāk k''ü-ti tsoi ko-ch''ü tso mät-ye</td></tr><tr><td>21 The sky is all blue</td><td>個天青嘥</td><td>ko t''in ts''ing sai</td></tr><tr><td>25 Did he come from Hongkong by ship?</td><td>佢喺香港搭船來係唔係</td><td>k''ü hai Heung-kong tap shün loi hai ''m hai?</td></tr><tr><td>26 Yes, he came in a large ship</td><td>係,佢搭隻大船來嘅</td><td>hai, k''ü tap chek tai shün loi ke</td></tr><tr><td>27 Who killed that man?</td><td>乜誰殺死响個人</td><td>mät-shui shat-sze ko-ko yan?</td></tr><tr><td>28 Four men killed him with swords</td><td>四個人俾刀殺死佢</td><td>sze ko yan pi to shat-sze k''ü</td></tr><tr><td>29 A large party of people were there</td><td>一隊人响處</td><td>yat tui yan heung ch''ü</td></tr><tr><td>30 A pull of wind came suddenly</td><td>一陣風忽然間吹來</td><td>yat chän fung fat-in-kan ch''ui loi</td></tr><tr><td>31 Take this letter and bring an answer</td><td>帶呢封信去攞回音翻來</td><td>tai ni fung-sän hü lo ui-yäm fan loi</td></tr><tr><td>32 Who gave you this answer?</td><td>乜誰俾回音過你呢</td><td>mät-shui pi ui-yäm kwo ni ni?</td></tr><tr><td>33 It he is not at his office, go to his house</td><td>若係佢唔在寫字樓,就去佢嘅屋</td><td>yeuk hai k''ü ''m tsoi se-tsz-lau, tsan hü k''ü ke uk</td></tr><tr><td>34 I don''t want you any longer</td><td>我唔使用你啲咁耐添咯</td><td>ngo ''m shai yung ni ti kom noi t''im lok</td></tr><tr><td>35 Tell him to wait, I am very busy</td><td>呌佢等吓,我十分唔得閒</td><td>kiu k''ü tǎng ha, ngo shap-fān ''m tǎk han</td></tr><tr><td>36 Go and see (ask) what that noise is</td><td>去問吓做乜野咁嘈</td><td>hü män ha tso-mät-ye kom ts''o</td></tr><tr><td>37 It is a little boy making a noise</td><td>响個細紋仔嘈呢</td><td>ko-ko sai-màn-tsai ts''o ni</td></tr><tr><td>38 Tell him he will be punished</td><td>話佢知,等吓責罰佢</td><td>wa k''ü chi, tǎng ha chak-fat k''ü</td></tr><tr><td>39 Have you walked to the school?</td><td>你有行路去書館冇</td><td>ni yau hang lo hü shü-kun mo?</td></tr><tr><td>40 No, I went in a carriage</td><td>唔係,我坐馬車去嘅</td><td>''m hai, ngo tso ma-ch''e hü ke</td></tr></table>', '<tableborder="1"><tr><td>23Iforgetwhattheydothere</td><td>我唔記得佢哋在响處做乜野</td><td>ngo''mki-tākk''ü-titsoiko-ch''ütsomät-ye</td></tr><tr><td>21Theskyisallblue</td><td>個天青嘥</td><td>kot''ints''ingsai</td></tr><tr><td>25DidhecomefromHongkongbyship?</td><td>佢喺香港搭船來係唔係</td><td>k''ühaiHeung-kongtapshünloihai''mhai?</td></tr><tr><td>26Yes,hecameinalargeship</td><td>係,佢搭隻大船來嘅</td><td>hai,k''ütapchektaishünloike</td></tr><tr><td>27Whokilledthatman?</td><td>乜誰殺死响個人</td><td>mät-shuishat-szeko-koyan?</td></tr><tr><td>28Fourmenkilledhimwithswords</td><td>四個人俾刀殺死佢</td><td>szekoyanpitoshat-szek''ü</td></tr><tr><td>29Alargepartyofpeoplewerethere</td><td>一隊人响處</td><td>yattuiyanheungch''ü</td></tr><tr><td>30Apullofwindcamesuddenly</td><td>一陣風忽然間吹來</td><td>yatchänfungfat-in-kanch''uiloi</td></tr><tr><td>31Takethisletterandbringananswer</td><td>帶呢封信去攞回音翻來</td><td>tainifung-sänhüloui-yämfanloi</td></tr><tr><td>32Whogaveyouthisanswer?</td><td>乜誰俾回音過你呢</td><td>mät-shuipiui-yämkwonini?</td></tr><tr><td>33Itheisnotathisoffice,gotohishouse</td><td>若係佢唔在寫字樓,就去佢嘅屋</td><td>yeukhaik''ü''mtsoise-tsz-lau,tsanhük''ükeuk</td></tr><tr><td>34Idon''twantyouanylonger</td><td>我唔使用你啲咁耐添咯</td><td>ngo''mshaiyungnitikomnoit''imlok</td></tr><tr><td>35Tellhimtowait,Iamverybusy</td><td>呌佢等吓,我十分唔得閒</td><td>kiuk''ütǎngha,ngoshap-fān''mtǎkhan</td></tr><tr><td>36Goandsee(ask)whatthatnoiseis</td><td>去問吓做乜野咁嘈</td><td>hümänhatso-mät-yekomts''o</td></tr><tr><td>37Itisalittleboymakinganoise</td><td>响個細紋仔嘈呢</td><td>ko-kosai-màn-tsaits''oni</td></tr><tr><td>38Tellhimhewillbepunished</td><td>話佢知,等吓責罰佢</td><td>wak''üchi,tǎnghachak-fatk''ü</td></tr><tr><td>39Haveyouwalkedtotheschool?</td><td>你有行路去書館冇</td><td>niyauhanglohüshü-kunmo?</td></tr><tr><td>40No,Iwentinacarriage</td><td>唔係,我坐馬車去嘅</td><td>''mhai,ngotsoma-ch''ehüke</td></tr></table>', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-087-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 87, 1, 'LESSON XXX.', '<table border="1"><tr><td>An account (bill)</td><td>一條數</td><td>yat t''iu sho''</td><td>To reckon up</td><td>計起</td><td>kai'' hi''</td></tr><tr><td>A church</td><td>福音堂</td><td>fuk-yäm-t''ong</td><td>To know</td><td>知到</td><td>chi to''</td></tr><tr><td>To dislike</td><td>唔中意</td><td>''m chung-i''</td><td>To waken</td><td>呌醒</td><td>kiu'' sing''</td></tr><tr><td>To choose, select</td><td>揀擇</td><td>kán''-chak</td><td>Moreover</td><td>而且</td><td>i-ch''e''</td></tr><tr><td>To anchor</td><td>抛錨</td><td>p''au nau</td><td>The mind (heart)</td><td>心</td><td>sǎm</td></tr><tr><td>A (street) barrier</td><td>街閘</td><td>kai-chap</td><td>Troops</td><td>兵</td><td>ping</td></tr><tr><td>To stop up</td><td>.塞住</td><td>suk chü''</td><td>To level</td><td>平</td><td>p''ing</td></tr><tr><td>To follow</td><td>跟住</td><td>kan chü''</td><td>Rope</td><td>繩</td><td>shing</td></tr></table>

Adjectives usually precede, or follow, the nouns they qualify as in English; e.g., a good horse, YAT P''AT HO MA 一匹好馬; this horse is good, NI P''AT MA HO, 呢匹馬好.

Many adjectives are formed from nouns by the addition of TI 啲; e.g., better HO TI 好啲, worse, inferior, YAI-TI 昕啲. As, however, TI 啲 when following an adjective expressing form, quality, colour, or space, usually signifies the comparative degree (as in SAI-TI 細啲 smaller, TAI-TI 大啲 larger, etc.) KE 嘅 is more frequently used for such adjectives in their positive sense, though TI 啲 is sometimes retained for the sake of euphony. When two adjectival words come together, TI 啲 or KE 嘅 is generally omitted; e.g., a rich man FU-KWAI YAN 富貴人, or TS''OI-CHÜ LO 財主佬.

Beautiful 好睇 ho'' t''ai Clean 乾淨 kon-tseng'' Poor 窮 k''ung

Do. 華美 wa-mi'' Wrong 錯 ts''oh'' Old 老 lo''

Rich 財主 ts''oi-chü'' Short 短 tün'' Hot 熱 it

That is middling响個係中中嘅啫 ko''-ko` hai` chung-chung ke` che

Read that book aloud大聲讀响溥書 tai` shing tuk ko'' po` shü

I want to go to sleep我愛去瞓咯 ngo'' oi` hü` fän` lok

I dare not do it我唔敢做 ngo'' ''m kom'' tso''

I dare not presume我唔敢當 ngo'' ''m kom'' tong

Wake him up呌醒佢 kiu` sing'' k''u''

