  ('cvh-088-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 88, 1, NULL, '<table border="1"><tr><td>To accompany friends</td><td>送朋友</td><td>sung'' p''āng-yau''</td></tr><tr><td>You are very good (kind)</td><td>你有心</td><td>ni'' yau'' sām</td></tr><tr><td>Wait for an answer</td><td>等回音</td><td>tǎng'' ni-yām</td></tr><tr><td>Speak loudly</td><td>大聲講</td><td>tai'' shing kong''</td></tr><tr><td>Wherelore?—what for?</td><td>爲乜野</td><td>wai''-màt-ye''</td></tr><tr><td>To visit a person</td><td>探人</td><td>t''am'' yan</td></tr></table>

<table border="1"><tr><td>Dining-room</td><td>大餐房</td><td>tai''-ts''an-fong</td><td>Scaffolding (bamboo)</td><td>竹棚</td><td>chuk-p''āng</td></tr><tr><td>Bath-room</td><td>洗身房</td><td>sai''-shān-fong</td><td>Study or library</td><td>書房</td><td>shü-fong</td></tr><tr><td>Bed-room</td><td>瞓房</td><td>fün''-fong</td><td>Flower-garden</td><td>花園</td><td>fu-ün</td></tr><tr><td>Steps</td><td>階級</td><td>kai-k''äp</td><td>Drawing-room</td><td>客廳</td><td>hak-t''eng</td></tr><tr><td>Lock</td><td>把鎖</td><td>pi''-soh''</td><td>Foundation</td><td>地脚</td><td>ti''-keuk</td></tr><tr><td>Key</td><td>鎖匙</td><td>soh''-shi</td><td>Brick wall</td><td>磚牆</td><td>chün ts''enug</td></tr><tr><td>Hinges</td><td>較</td><td>kuu''</td><td>Mud wall</td><td>坭牆</td><td>nai ts''eung</td></tr><tr><td>Wall</td><td>牆</td><td>ts''eung</td><td>God (the Creator)</td><td>上帝</td><td>sheung''tai''</td></tr></table>

Considerable discussion—extending to the publication of entire volumes devoted to the subject—has arisen as to the best Chinese equivalent for the word "God." That above given is now adopted by the majority of sinologues.

All, when used substantively in the sense of a relative pronoun, is idiomatically expressed by YAT KO TO 一個都.

Both and are expressed by YAU 又——YAU 又; e.g., they are all both old and poor, YAT KO TO HAI YAU LO YAU K''UNG 一個都係又老又窮.

<table border="1"><tr><td>1 Are those steps short or long?</td><td>响啲階級係長只短呢</td><td>ko-ti kai-k''ap hai ch''enng chi tün ni?</td></tr><tr><td>2 Where did the boat anchor?</td><td>响隻船抛在邊處</td><td>ko chek shün p''au tsoi pin-ch''ü?</td></tr><tr><td>3 He went to the beautiful garden</td><td>佢去响間華美嘅花園處</td><td>k''ü hui ko kan wa-mi ke fa-ün ch''ü</td></tr><tr><td>4 It was very hot yesterday; to-day it is warm</td><td>昨日好熱,今日煖啫</td><td>tsok-yat ho it; kām-yat nūn che</td></tr><tr><td>5 Why do you dislike the people?</td><td>爲乜事你唔中意人哋呢</td><td>wai-mât-sze ni ''m chung-i yan ti ni?</td></tr><tr><td>6 Tell him to reckon up the bill</td><td>呌佢計起响張單</td><td>kiu k''ü kai-hi ko cheung tan</td></tr><tr><td>7 My house has a dining-room and a bed-room</td><td>我嘅屋有間大餐房共間瞓房</td><td>ngo ke nk yan kan tai-ts''an-fong kung kan làn-fong</td></tr></table>', '<tableborder="1"><tr><td>Toaccompanyfriends</td><td>送朋友</td><td>sung''p''āng-yau''</td></tr><tr><td>Youareverygood(kind)</td><td>你有心</td><td>ni''yau''sām</td></tr><tr><td>Waitforananswer</td><td>等回音</td><td>tǎng''ni-yām</td></tr><tr><td>Speakloudly</td><td>大聲講</td><td>tai''shingkong''</td></tr><tr><td>Wherelore?—whatfor?</td><td>爲乜野</td><td>wai''-màt-ye''</td></tr><tr><td>Tovisitaperson</td><td>探人</td><td>t''am''yan</td></tr></table><tableborder="1"><tr><td>Dining-room</td><td>大餐房</td><td>tai''-ts''an-fong</td><td>Scaffolding(bamboo)</td><td>竹棚</td><td>chuk-p''āng</td></tr><tr><td>Bath-room</td><td>洗身房</td><td>sai''-shān-fong</td><td>Studyorlibrary</td><td>書房</td><td>shü-fong</td></tr><tr><td>Bed-room</td><td>瞓房</td><td>fün''-fong</td><td>Flower-garden</td><td>花園</td><td>fu-ün</td></tr><tr><td>Steps</td><td>階級</td><td>kai-k''äp</td><td>Drawing-room</td><td>客廳</td><td>hak-t''eng</td></tr><tr><td>Lock</td><td>把鎖</td><td>pi''-soh''</td><td>Foundation</td><td>地脚</td><td>ti''-keuk</td></tr><tr><td>Key</td><td>鎖匙</td><td>soh''-shi</td><td>Brickwall</td><td>磚牆</td><td>chünts''enug</td></tr><tr><td>Hinges</td><td>較</td><td>kuu''</td><td>Mudwall</td><td>坭牆</td><td>naits''eung</td></tr><tr><td>Wall</td><td>牆</td><td>ts''eung</td><td>God(theCreator)</td><td>上帝</td><td>sheung''tai''</td></tr></table>Considerablediscussion—extendingtothepublicationofentirevolumesdevotedtothesubject—hasarisenastothebestChineseequivalentfortheword"God."Thatabovegivenisnowadoptedbythemajorityofsinologues.All,whenusedsubstantivelyinthesenseofarelativepronoun,isidiomaticallyexpressedbyYATKOTO一個都.BothandareexpressedbyYAU又——YAU又;e.g.,theyareallbotholdandpoor,YATKOTOHAIYAULOYAUK''UNG一個都係又老又窮.<tableborder="1"><tr><td>1Arethosestepsshortorlong?</td><td>响啲階級係長只短呢</td><td>ko-tikai-k''aphaich''enngchitünni?</td></tr><tr><td>2Wheredidtheboatanchor?</td><td>响隻船抛在邊處</td><td>kochekshünp''autsoipin-ch''ü?</td></tr><tr><td>3Hewenttothebeautifulgarden</td><td>佢去响間華美嘅花園處</td><td>k''ühuikokanwa-mikefa-ünch''ü</td></tr><tr><td>4Itwasveryhotyesterday;to-dayitiswarm</td><td>昨日好熱,今日煖啫</td><td>tsok-yathoit;kām-yatnūnche</td></tr><tr><td>5Whydoyoudislikethepeople?</td><td>爲乜事你唔中意人哋呢</td><td>wai-mât-szeni''mchung-iyantini?</td></tr><tr><td>6Tellhimtoreckonupthebill</td><td>呌佢計起响張單</td><td>kiuk''ükai-hikocheungtan</td></tr><tr><td>7Myhousehasadining-roomandabed-room</td><td>我嘅屋有間大餐房共間瞓房</td><td>ngokenkyankantai-ts''an-fongkungkanlàn-fong</td></tr></table>', 'verified'),
