finishedwriting</td><td>我寫完咯</td><td>ngo''se''ünlok</td></tr><tr><td>Assistme</td><td>帮助我</td><td>pongcho''ngo''</td></tr><tr><td>Don''ttroubleme</td><td>咪混我</td><td>mai''wan''ngo''</td></tr></table>', 'needs_review'),
  ('cvh-092-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 92, 1, NULL, '<table border="1"><tr><td>Tea is ready</td><td>茶便咯</td><td>ch''a pin'' lok</td></tr><tr><td>Let it alone</td><td>咪門佢</td><td>mai'' tau'' k''ü''</td></tr><tr><td>Don''t injure him (or it)</td><td>咪害佢</td><td>mai'' hoi'' k''ü''</td></tr><tr><td>Don''t fear</td><td>唔使怕</td><td>''m shai'' p''a''</td></tr><tr><td>Step aside a little</td><td>行開啲</td><td>hang hoi ti</td></tr><tr><td>Don''t fall down</td><td>咪跌倒</td><td>mai'' tit to''</td></tr><tr><td>I am afraid to speak</td><td>我怕講</td><td>ngo'' p''a'' kong''</td></tr><tr><td>Of no use</td><td>冇用嘅</td><td>mo'' yung'' ke''</td></tr><tr><td>To put on again</td><td>着番</td><td>cheuk fan</td></tr></table>

<table border="1"><tr><td>Office</td><td>寫字房</td><td>se''-tsz''-fong</td><td>Window</td><td>窓門</td><td>ch''eung-mun</td></tr><tr><td>Ceiling</td><td>天花板</td><td>t''in-fu-pan''</td><td>Horse-whip</td><td>馬鞕</td><td>ma''-pin</td></tr><tr><td>Blinds</td><td>百葉窓</td><td>pak-ip-ch''eung</td><td>A saddle</td><td>馬鞍</td><td>ma''-on</td></tr><tr><td>The floor</td><td>地台板</td><td>ti''-t''oi-pan''</td><td>Bridle</td><td>馬韁</td><td>ma''-keung</td></tr><tr><td>Stirrup</td><td>馬踏橈</td><td>ma''-tap-tang''</td><td>Roof</td><td>瓦背</td><td>nga''-pui''</td></tr><tr><td>Partition</td><td>板帳</td><td>pan''-cheung''</td><td>Do.</td><td>瓦面</td><td>nga''-min''</td></tr><tr><td>Kitchen</td><td>廚房</td><td>ch''ü-fong</td><td>Window</td><td>窓</td><td>ch''eung</td></tr><tr><td>Chimney</td><td>烟通</td><td>in-t''ung</td><td>Tiles</td><td>瓦</td><td>nga''</td></tr></table>

The accusative (objective) following an active verb is sometimes preceded by TSEUNG 將 (here meaning to take) and is then placed first in the sentence; e.g., put that horse-whip down there TSEUNG KO CHI MA-PIN FONG HA KO-CH''ü 將响枝馬鞭放下個處.

<table border="1"><tr><td>1 Assist me to pacify that man</td><td>帮助我和息响個人</td><td>pong cho ngo woh sik ko-ko yan</td></tr><tr><td>2 We cannot prevent his doing it so</td><td>我哋不能阻住佢噉做</td><td>ngo-ti păt nǎng choh chü k''ü kom tso</td></tr><tr><td>3 Go and pull on that rope</td><td>去扯住個條繩</td><td>hü ch''e chü ko t''iu shing</td></tr><tr><td>4 Does he work in silver or gold?</td><td>佢打金只打銀呢</td><td>k''ü ta kām chi ta ngăn ni?</td></tr><tr><td>5 Has your office a chimney?</td><td>你嘅寫字房有個烟通冇</td><td>ni ke se-tsz-fong yau ko in-t''ung mo?</td></tr><tr><td>6 No, my kitchen has a chimney and two windows</td><td>唔係,我嘅廚房有個烟通及兩度窓門</td><td>''m hai, ngo ke ch''ü-fong yau ko in-t''ung k''ap leung to ch''eung-mun</td></tr></table>', '<tableborder="1"><tr><td>Teaisready</td><td>茶便咯</td><td>ch''apin''lok</td></tr><tr><td>Letitalone</td><td>咪門佢</td><td>mai''tau''k''ü''</td></tr><tr><td>Don''tinjurehim(orit)</td><td>咪害佢</td><td>mai''hoi''k''ü''</td></tr><tr><td>Don''tfear</td><td>唔使怕</td><td>''mshai''p''a''</td></tr><tr><td>Stepasidealittle</td><td>行開啲</td><td>hanghoiti</td></tr><tr><td>Don''tfalldown</td><td>咪跌倒</td><td>mai''titto''</td></tr><tr><td>Iamafraidtospeak</td><td>我怕講</td><td>ngo''p''a''kong''</td></tr><tr><td>Ofnouse</td><td>冇用嘅</td><td>mo''yung''ke''</td></tr><tr><td>Toputonagain</td><td>着番</td><td>cheukfan</td></tr></table><tableborder="1"><tr><td>Office</td><td>寫字房</td><td>se''-tsz''-fong</td><td>Window</td><td>窓門</td><td>ch''eung-mun</td></tr><tr><td>Ceiling</td><td>天花板</td><td>t''in-fu-pan''</td><td>Horse-whip</td><td>馬鞕</td><td>ma''-pin</td></tr><tr><td>Blinds</td><td>百葉窓</td><td>pak-ip-ch''eung</td><td>Asaddle</td><td>馬鞍</td><td>ma''-on</td></tr><tr><td>Thefloor</td><td>地台板</td><td>ti''-t''oi-pan''</td><td>Bridle</td><td>馬韁</td><td>ma''-keung</td></tr><tr><td>Stirrup</td><td>馬踏橈</td><td>ma''-tap-tang''</td><td>Roof</td><td>瓦背</td><td>nga''-pui''</td></tr><tr><td>Partition</td><td>板帳</td><td>pan''-cheung''</td><td>Do.</td><td>瓦面</td><td>nga''-min''</td></tr><tr><td>Kitchen</td><td>廚房</td><td>ch''ü-fong</td><td>Window</td><td>窓</td><td>ch''eung</td></tr><tr><td>Chimney</td><td>烟通</td><td>in-t''ung</td><td>Tiles</td><td>瓦</td><td>nga''</td></tr></table>Theaccusative(objective)followinganactiveverbissometimesprecededbyTSEUNG將(heremeaningtotake)andisthenplacedfirstinthesentence;e.g.,putthathorse-whipdownthereTSEUNGKOCHIMA-PINFONGHAKO-CH''ü將响枝馬鞭放下個處.<tableborder="1"><tr><td>1Assistmetopacifythatman</td><td>帮助我和息响個人</td><td>pongchongowohsikko-koyan</td></tr><tr><td>2Wecannotpreventhisdoingitso</td><td>我哋不能阻住佢噉做</td><td>ngo-tipătnǎngchohchük''ükomtso</td></tr><tr><td>3Goandpullonthatrope</td><td>去扯住個條繩</td><td>hüch''echükot''iushing</td></tr><tr><td>4Doesheworkinsilverorgold?</td><td>佢打金只打銀呢</td><td>k''ütakāmchitangănni?</td></tr><tr><td>5Hasyourofficeachimney?</td><td>你嘅寫字房有個烟通冇</td><td>nikese-tsz-fongyaukoin-t''ungmo?</td></tr><tr><td>6No,mykitchenhasachimneyandtwowindows</td><td>唔係,我嘅廚房有個烟通及兩度窓門</td><td>''mhai,ngokech''ü-fongyaukoin-t''ungk''apleungtoch''eung-mun</td></tr></table>', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-093-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 93, 1, NULL, '7 You must have some blinds 你是必有的百葉窓 ni shi-pit yau ti pak-ip-ch''eung

8 There are a good many tiles 瓦背面有好多 nga-pui min yau ho to nga on the roof 瓦

9 Tell the coolie to sweep the 叫個管店掃响個地 kiu ko kun-tim so ko-ko ti-t''oi floor 台板 pan

10 Can you reach it with your 你用手可以擙得到 ni yung shau ho i o tāk to ''m hands 唔呢 ni?

11 I want a saddle and a bridle 我要個馬鞍及馬韁 ngo iu ko ma-on k''ap ma-keung

12 Run after that man and get 追到响個人攞番我 chui to ko-ko yan lo fan ngo ke my stirrups 嘅馬踏橙 ma-tap-tüng

13 Send my horsewhip to me 寄我嘅馬鞭嚟我 ki ngo ke ma-pin lai ngo

14 The horses drag the carriage 馬拉車 ma lai ch''e

15 He is a wealthy man, but not 佢係有錢嘅人, 但 k''ü hai yan ts''in ke yan, tan ''m amiable 唔係可愛嘅 hai ho oi ke

16 Here are some lumps of earth 呢處有幾堆坭 ni-ch''ü yau ki tui nai

17 There are several willows there 個處有幾窠柳樹 ko-ch''ü yau ki p''o lau-shü

18 Has that boat a sail? 個隻艇有堂𢃇冇 ko chek t''ing yau t''ong li mo?

19 I must buy a mosquito 我要買堂蚊帳 ngo iu mai t''ong măn-cheung curtain

20 He uses very bad language 佢用十分爛口 k''ü yung shap-fan lan hau

21 That is of no use 响的有用嘅 ko-ti mo yung ke

22 He is a hateful man ; but don''t 佢係一個可恨嘅人 ; k''ü hai yat ko ho-han ke yan ;

injure him 但唔好害佢 tan ''m ho boi k''ü

