  ('cvh-106-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 106, 1, 'LESSON XXXV.', '<table><tr><td>To insert</td><td>放入</td><td>fong'' yap</td><td>To arrest, appre-</td><td>捉住</td><td>chak chu</td></tr><tr><td>To kick</td><td>踢起</td><td>t''ek hi''</td><td>hend (seize)</td><td>拿住</td><td>na chu''</td></tr><tr><td>To lock up</td><td>鎖起</td><td>soh'' hi''</td><td>To cover</td><td>蓋住</td><td>k''oi'' chu''</td></tr><tr><td>To leap or jump</td><td>跳起</td><td>t''iu'' hi''</td><td>To descend</td><td>落去</td><td>lok hui</td></tr><tr><td>To lift up</td><td>摠起</td><td>tau hi''</td><td>To fly away</td><td>飛去</td><td>fi hui</td></tr><tr><td>To carry (children)</td><td>抱住</td><td>p''o'' chü''</td><td>A play (drama)</td><td>戲</td><td>hi''</td></tr><tr><td>To rest from</td><td>歇住</td><td>hit chü''</td><td>To hope</td><td>望</td><td>mong</td></tr><tr><td>To reflect upon</td><td>顧住</td><td>ku'' chü''</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table>

The verb to rest from is applied to the agent and not to the act; e.g., to rest from work is "to cease with the hand" HIT CHU SHAU 歇住手; to stop eating HIT CHÜ HAU 歇住口 (rest the mouth.)

<table><tr><td>An affair</td><td>一宗事</td><td>yat tsung sze</td><td>A flagstaff</td><td>旗杆</td><td>k''i-kon</td></tr><tr><td>A map</td><td>地理圖</td><td>ti`-li''-t''o</td><td>The legs</td><td>大脾</td><td>tai`-pi''</td></tr><tr><td>A weight</td><td>稱,杯</td><td>ch''ing'', p''ing</td><td>An enemy</td><td>仇敵</td><td>ch''au-tik</td></tr><tr><td>Children (ba-</td><td>孩兒</td><td>hoi-i</td><td>Robbers</td><td>賊匪</td><td>ts''ak-fi''</td></tr><tr><td colspan="3">bies; more generally applied to males)</td><td>The eyes</td><td>眼</td><td>ngan''</td></tr></table>

In addition to the forms of personal and possessive pronouns already given in previous lessons, there are several substitutes in polite colloquial. A person speaking of his own relations uses either a descriptive or depreciatory phrase. Of the former the following are examples.

<table><tr><td>My father</td><td>父親</td><td>fu''-ts''uo</td></tr><tr><td>Do..</td><td>家父</td><td>ka-fu''</td></tr><tr><td>My elder brother</td><td>家兄</td><td>ka-hing</td></tr><tr><td>My younger (cottage) brother</td><td>舍弟</td><td>she''tai''</td></tr><tr><td>My wife</td><td>老婆</td><td>lo''-p''oh</td></tr><tr><td>Do.</td><td>内人</td><td>noi''yan</td></tr><tr><td>Do.</td><td>内室</td><td>noi''shat</td></tr></table>

