  ('cvh-135-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 135, 1, NULL, '<table border="1"><tr><td>28 You must exert yourself to read</td><td>你是必要盡力讀書噃</td><td>ni shi-pit iu tsun-lik tuk shü poh</td></tr><tr><td>29 You will find it difficult to learn Chinese</td><td>你將來就知得學唐話係難咯</td><td>ni tseung-loi tsau chi täk hok T‘ong-wa hai nan lok</td></tr><tr><td>30 Who gave you those chairs?</td><td>乜誰俾响啲椅過你嘅呢</td><td>măt-shui pi ko-ti i kwo ni ke ni?</td></tr><tr><td>31 A certain friend of mine gave them to me</td><td>有一個朋友俾過我嘅</td><td>yau yat ko p‘ang-yau pi kwo ngo ke</td></tr><tr><td>32 Have you not yet seen him?</td><td>你未曾見過佢咩</td><td>ni mi ts‘äng kin kwo k‘ü me?</td></tr><tr><td>33 I have seen him a few times only</td><td>我見過佢幾次啫</td><td>ngo kin kwo k‘ü ki ts‘z che</td></tr><tr><td>34 Have many visitors come today?</td><td>今日有好多人客來咩</td><td>kam-yat yau ho to yan-hak lei me?</td></tr><tr><td>35 Not many to day;I expect a great many to-morrow</td><td>今日冇幾多啫;聽日怕多啲</td><td>kam-yat mo ki to che;t’eng-yat p’a to ti</td></tr><tr><td>36 Exert yourself to do that properly</td><td>盡力做妥當响啲</td><td>tsun-lik tso t‘oh tong ko-ti</td></tr><tr><td>37 There is nothing said about him</td><td>冇乜野話到佢呀</td><td>mo măt-ye wa to k‘ü a</td></tr><tr><td>38 Such conduct is most improper</td><td>噉樣嘅行爲係極唔合嘅</td><td>kom yeung ke hang-wai hai kik ’m hop ke</td></tr><tr><td>39 Every thing is exactly as I like it</td><td>各樣都係十分中我意嘅咯</td><td>kok yeung to hai shap-fān chung ngo i ke lok</td></tr></table>', '<tableborder="1"><tr><td>28Youmustexertyourselftoread</td><td>你是必要盡力讀書噃</td><td>nishi-pitiutsun-liktukshüpoh</td></tr><tr><td>29YouwillfinditdifficulttolearnChinese</td><td>你將來就知得學唐話係難咯</td><td>nitseung-loitsauchitäkhokT‘ong-wahainanlok</td></tr><tr><td>30Whogaveyouthosechairs?</td><td>乜誰俾响啲椅過你嘅呢</td><td>măt-shuipiko-tiikwonikeni?</td></tr><tr><td>31Acertainfriendofminegavethemtome</td><td>有一個朋友俾過我嘅</td><td>yauyatkop‘ang-yaupikwongoke</td></tr><tr><td>32Haveyounotyetseenh