  ('cvh-143-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 143, 1, NULL, '<table border="1"><tr><td>32</td><td>He uses a shaving brush when he shaves people</td><td>佢同人剃頭時，用個水抆掃</td><td>k&#x27;ü t&#x27;ung yan t&#x27;ai t&#x27;au shi yung ko shui-män-so</td></tr><tr><td>33</td><td>What goods are on board the merchant vessel?</td><td>嗰隻貨船載有乜野貨呢</td><td>ko chek foh-shün tsoi yau măt-ye foh ni?</td></tr><tr><td>34</td><td>She has guns and ammunition (ma&#x27;-tsz&#x27;)</td><td>佢有鎗砲共碼子</td><td>k&#x27;ü yau ts&#x27;eung p&#x27;au kung ma-tsz</td></tr><tr><td>35</td><td>Are there many Spaniards at that place?</td><td>嗰處有好多呂宋人咩</td><td>ko ch&#x27;ü yau ho to Lü-sung yan me?</td></tr><tr><td>36</td><td>No, but there are several Chinese and Englishmen</td><td>冇，但有幾個唐人共英國人啫</td><td>mo, tan yau ki ko T&#x27;ong-yan kung Ying-kwok yan che</td></tr><tr><td>37</td><td>Did all the birds fly away?</td><td>咁多雀都飛嘥去咩</td><td>kom to tseuk to fi sai hü me?</td></tr><tr><td>38</td><td>You should have taken more care</td><td>你應該子細啲</td><td>ni ying-koi tsz-sai ti</td></tr><tr><td>39</td><td>There is a disagreement between these two men</td><td>嗰兩個人嘅心十分不一</td><td>ko leung ko yan ke sam shap-fān pat yat</td></tr><tr><td>40</td><td>A whole life is not enough to do it in</td><td>一世都唔做得嘥嘅</td><td>yat shai to &#x27;m tso tãk sai ke</td></tr></table>', '<tableborder="1"><tr><td>32</td><td>Heusesashavingbrushwhenheshavespeople</td><td>佢同人剃頭時，用個水抆掃</td><td>k&#x27;üt&#x27;ungyant&#x27;ait&#x27;aushiyungkoshui-män-so</td></tr><tr><td>33</td><td>Whatgoodsareonboardthemerchantvessel?</td><td>嗰隻貨船載有乜野貨呢</td><td>kochekfoh-shüntsoiyaumăt-yefohni?</td></tr><tr><td>34</td><td>Shehasgunsandammunition(ma&#x27;-tsz&#x27;)</td><td>佢有鎗砲共碼子</td><td>k&#x27;üyauts&#x27;eungp&#x27;aukungma-tsz</td></tr><tr><td>35</td><td>AretheremanySpaniardsatthatplace?</td><td>嗰處有好多呂宋人咩</td><td>koch&#x27;üyauhotoLü-sungyanme?</td></tr><tr><td>36</td><td>No,butthereareseveralChineseandEnglishmen</td><td>冇，但有幾個唐人共英國人啫</td><td>mo,tanyaukikoT&#x27;ong-yankungYing-kwokyanche</td></tr><tr><td>37</td><td>Didallthebirdsflyaway?</td><td>咁多雀都飛嘥去咩</td><td>komtotseuktofisaihüme?</td></tr><tr><td>38</td><td>Youshouldhavetakenmorecare</td><td>你應該子細啲</td><td>niying-koitsz-saiti</td></tr><tr><td>39</td><td>Thereisadisagreementbetweenthesetwomen</td><td>嗰兩個人嘅心十分不一</td><td>koleungkoyankesamshap-fānpatyat</td></tr><tr><td>40</td><td>Awholelifeisnotenoughtodoitin</td><td>一世都唔做得嘥嘅</td><td>yatshaito&#x27;mtsotãksaike</td></tr></table>', 'needs_review'),
  ('cvh-143-02', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 143, 2, 'LESSON XLV.', '<table border="1"><tr><td>To use one ill</td><td>刻薄待人</td><td>hak-pok toi&#x27; yan</td><td>To mix together</td><td>攪埋</td><td>kau&#x27;-mai</td></tr><tr><td>No help for it</td><td>冇奈何</td><td>mo&#x27;-noi&#x27;-ho</td><td>To empty</td><td>倒空</td><td>to&#x27;-hung</td></tr><tr><td>Oblige me</td><td>爲吓我</td><td>wai&#x27; ha&#x27; ngo&#x27;</td><td>To turn out</td><td>倒出</td><td>to&#x27;-ch&#x27;ut</td></tr><tr><td>Secretly</td><td>私私啲</td><td>sze-sze-ti</td><td>Fireworks</td><td>烟火</td><td>in-foh&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="2">To turn inside out</td><td rowspan="2">翻裏面出嚟</td><td>fan&#x27; li&#x27;-min&#x27;</td><td>To let off fireworks</td><td>燒烟火</td><td>shiu in-foh&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>ch&#x27;ut lai</td><td>To look after</td><td>看住</td><td>hon-chü&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>To turn upside down</td><td>倒轉</td><td>to&#x27;-chün&#x27;</td><td>To care for</td><td>睇顧</td><td>t&#x27;ai-ku&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>A mosquito net</td><td>蚊袋</td><td>mian-toi&#x27;</td><td>Do.</td><td>照料</td><td>chin&#x27;-liu&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>The least bit</td><td>至少</td><td>chi shiu&#x27;</td><td>Do.</td><td>顧住</td><td>ku&#x27;-chu&#x27;</td></tr></table>', '<tableborder="1"><tr><td>Touseoneill</td><td>刻薄待人</td><td>hak-poktoi&#x27;yan</td><td>Tomixtogether</td><td>攪埋</td><td>kau&#x27;-mai</td></tr><tr><td>Nohelpforit</td><td>冇奈何</td><td>mo&#x27;-noi&#x27;-ho</td><td>Toempty</td><td>倒空</td><td>to&#x27;-hung</td></tr><tr><td>Obligeme</td><td>爲吓我</td><td>wai&#x27;ha&#x27;ngo&#x27;</td><td>Toturnout</td><td>倒出</td><td>to&#x27;-ch&#x27;ut</td></tr><tr><td>Secretly</td><td>私私啲</td><td>sze-sze-ti</td><td>Fireworks</td><td>烟火</td><td>in-foh&#x27;</td></tr><tr><tdrowspan="2">Toturninsideout</td><tdrowspan="2">翻裏面出嚟</td><td>fan&#x27;li&#x27;-min&#x27;</td><td>Toletofffireworks</td><td>燒烟火</td><td>shiuin-foh&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>ch&#x27;utlai</td><td>Tolookafter</td><td>看住</td><td>hon-chü&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Toturnupsidedown</td><td>倒轉</td><td>to&#x27;-chün&#x27;</td><td>Tocarefor</td><td>睇顧</td><td>t&#x27;ai-ku&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Amosquitonet</td><td>蚊袋</td><td>mian-toi&#x27;</td><td>Do.</td><td>照料</td><td>chin&#x27;-liu&#x27;</td></tr><tr><td>Theleastbit</td><td>至少</td><td>chishiu&#x27;</td><td>Do.</td><td>顧住</td><td>ku&#x27;-chu&#x27;</td></tr></table>', 'needs_review'),
  ('cvh-144-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 144, 1, NULL, 'The word PAK百, one hundred, is frequently used to express a collective quality or quantity; e.g., PAK-SING百姓 (lit. the hundred names) the people; PAK MUK百木 all the trees; PAK TS''IN MAN百千萬 an immense number.

MAN 萬 a myriad is used in the same sense; e.g. MAN-KWOK 萬國 all nations; MAN-FONG 萬方 all parts of the world; MAN-SUI 萬歲 for all years. The Emperor is addressed as MAN-SUI-YE 萬歲爺 (thousand years'' sire!) a million is expressed by YAT PAK MAN 一百萬, or YAT CHIU 一兆.

ORDINAL NUMBERS.

The ordinal numbers are expressed by prefixing TAI 第 before the cardinal numbers; e.g. the first TAI YAT 第一, the second TAI I 第二, &c.

The first who is expressed by sin 先——ke 嘅；e.g. the first who arrived, SIN TO KE 先到嘅.

The last who is expressed by SHAU MI 收尾——KE 嘅；e.g. the last who arrived SHAU MI TO KE 收尾到嘅.

When used to express the quality of goods the words first and second are rendered by SHEUNG 上 and CHUNG 中; e.g. first quality of rice SHEUNG MAI 上米; second do. CHUNG MAI 中米.

Firstly and secondly (or then) as applied to actions, are expressed by the simple ordinals.

<table><tr><td>They forgot it</td><td>佢哋忘記咯</td><td>k''ü''-ti'' mong-ki'' lok</td></tr><tr><td>We took medicine</td><td>我哋食曉藥</td><td>ngo''-ti'' shik hiu yeuk</td></tr><tr><td>Have you any more?</td><td>你重有冇呢</td><td>ni'' chung'' yau'' mo'' ni?</td></tr><tr><td>Anything will do</td><td>乜野都好</td><td>mát-ye'' to ho''</td></tr><tr><td>Don''t trouble me</td><td>咪煩我喇</td><td>mai'' fan ngo'' lo</td></tr><tr><td>Useless</td><td>冇乜用嘅</td><td>mo'' mät yung'' ke''</td></tr><tr><td>It can''t last long</td><td>不能長久</td><td>pat nāng ch''eung kau''</td></tr><tr><td>Of no importance</td><td>冇乜相干</td><td>mo'' mät seung-kon</td></tr><tr><td>Does it pain you?</td><td>令你痛咩</td><td>ling'' ni'' t''ung'' me?</td></tr><tr><td>Is it swollen?</td><td>有腫冇呀</td><td>yau'' chung'' mo'' a?</td></tr><tr><td>It leaks there</td><td>嗰處漏水</td><td>ko''-ch''ü'' lau'' shui''</td></tr><tr><td>Look in the dictionary</td><td>查字典</td><td>ch''a tsz''-tin''</td></tr></table>

Dressing-gown 修飾衫 sau-shik-sham Button hole 鈕扣 nau''-k''au''

Night-gown 墊瞓衫 tin-fun-sham Garters 襪帶 mat-ta''i

Pin 鼓槌針 ku''-ch''ui-cham gloves 手笠 shau''-lap', 'ThewordPAK百,onehundred,isfrequentlyusedtoexpressacollectivequalityorquantity;e.g.,PAK-SING百姓(lit.thehundrednames)thepeople;PAKMUK百木allthetrees;PAKTS''INMAN百千萬animmensenumber.MAN萬amyriadisusedinthesamesense;e.g.MAN-KWOK萬國allnations;MAN-FONG萬方allpartsoftheworld;MAN-SUI萬歲forallyears.TheEmperorisaddressedasMAN-SUI-YE萬歲爺(thousandyears''sire!)amillionisexpressedbyYATPAKMAN一百萬,orYATCHIU一兆.ORDINALNUMBERS.TheordinalnumbersareexpressedbyprefixingTAI第beforethecardinalnumbers;e.g.thefirstTAIYAT第一,thesecondTAII第二,&c.Thefirstwhoisexpressedbysin先——ke嘅；e.g.thefirstwhoarrived,SINTOKE先到嘅.ThelastwhoisexpressedbySHAUMI收尾——KE嘅；e.g.thelastwhoarrivedSHAUMITOKE收尾到嘅.WhenusedtoexpressthequalityofgoodsthewordsfirstandsecondarerenderedbySHEUNG上andCHUNG中;e.g.firstqualityofriceSHEUNGMAI上米;seconddo.CHUNGMAI中米.Firstlyandsecondly(orthen)asappliedtoactions,areexpressedbythesimpleordinals.<table><tr><td>Theyforgotit</td><td>佢哋忘記咯</td><td>k''ü''-ti''mong-ki''lok</td></tr><tr><td>Wetookmedicine</td><td>我哋食曉藥</td><td>ngo''-ti''shikhiuyeuk</td></tr><tr><td>Haveyouanymore?</td><td>你重有冇呢</td><td>ni''chung''yau''mo''ni?</td></tr><tr><td>Anythingwilldo</td><td>乜野都好</td><td>mát-ye''toho''</td></tr><tr><td>Don''ttroubleme</td><td>咪煩我喇</td><td>mai''fanngo''lo</td></tr><tr><td>Useless</td><td>冇乜用嘅</td><td>mo''mätyung''ke''</td></tr><tr><td>Itcan''tlastlong</td><td>不能長久</td><td>patnāngch''eungkau''</td></tr><tr><td>Ofnoimportance</td><td>冇乜相干</td><td>mo''mätseung-kon</td></tr><tr><td>Doesitpainyou?</td><td>令你痛咩</td><td>ling''ni''t''ung''me?</td></tr><tr><td>Isitswollen?</td><td>有腫冇呀</td><td>yau''chung''mo''a?</td></tr><tr><td>Itleaksthere</td><td>嗰處漏水</td><td>ko''-ch''ü''lau''shui''</td></tr><tr><td>Lookinthedictionary</td><td>查字典</td><td>ch''atsz''-tin''</td></tr></table>Dressing-gown修飾衫sau-shik-shamButtonhole鈕扣nau''-k''au''Night-gown墊瞓衫tin-fun-shamGarters襪帶mat-ta''iPin鼓槌針ku''-ch''ui-chamgloves手笠shau''-lap', 'needs_review'),
  ('cvh-145-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 145, 1, NULL, '<table><tr><td>Head dress</td><td>首飾</td><td>shau''-shik</td><td>Petticoat</td><td>裙</td><td>kw''an</td></tr><tr><td>Night cap</td><td>瞓帽</td><td>fün''mo''</td><td>Button</td><td>鈕</td><td>nau''</td></tr><tr><td>Pocket</td><td>衣袋</td><td>i-toi''</td><td>bag</td><td>袋</td><td>toi''</td></tr></table>

<table border="1"><tr><td>Apron</td><td>圍裙</td><td>wai-kw&#x27;an</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>The people use him ill</td><td>個啲百姓刻薄待佢</td><td>ko-ti pak-sing hak-pok toi k&#x27;ü</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Does he care for his friends?</td><td>佢顧住佢嘅朋友唔呢</td><td>k&#x27;ü ku-chü k&#x27;ü ke p&#x27;ang-yau &#x27;m ni?</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>He emptied the wooden tub</td><td>佢倒清嗰個木桶</td><td>k&#x27;ü to-ts&#x27;ing ko-ko muk-t&#x27;ung</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Tell him to mix the medicine</td><td>叫佢攪勻嗰啲藥</td><td>kiu k&#x27;ü kau-wän ko-ti yeuk</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Turn the box upside down</td><td>倒轉個箱底向上</td><td>to-chün ko seung tai heung sheung</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Turn the bag inside out</td><td>翻轉個袋裏面出嚟</td><td>fan-chün ko toi li-min ch&#x27;ut lai</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Don&#x27;t spoil that hat</td><td>咪整壞個頂帽</td><td>mai ching-wai ko ting mo</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Put the mosquito net over the bed</td><td>擠個蚊袋在床上</td><td>chai ko măn-toi tsoi ch&#x27;ong-sheung</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>All nations use clothes</td><td>萬國都用衣服嘅</td><td>man-kwok to yung i-fuk ke</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>I am afraid there is no help for it</td><td>我怕冇奈何咯</td><td>ngo p&#x27;a mo-noi-ho lok</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>Oblige me by doing this</td><td>爲吓我做呢啲喇</td><td>wai ha ngo tso ni-ti la</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>Men wear coats, and women wear petticoats</td><td>男人着長衫.女人着裙</td><td>nam-yan cheuk ch&#x27;eung-sham, nü-yan cheuk kw&#x27;an</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>You should not do that secretly</td><td>你私私啲做唔合理</td><td>ni sze-sze-ti tso &#x27;m hop li</td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td>You have written all those characters wrong</td><td>你寫錯嘥個啲字咯</td><td>ni se ts&#x27;oh sai ko-ti tsz lok</td></tr><tr><td>15</td><td>Tell the boy to hold my horse</td><td>叫個事仔牽住我匹馬</td><td>kiu ko sze-tsai hin chü ngo p&#x27;at ma</td></tr><tr><td>16</td><td>Do they let off fireworks?</td><td>佢哋燒烟火咩</td><td>k&#x27;ü-ti shiu in-foh me?</td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>Which (man) arrived first?</td><td>乜誰先到呢</td><td>mät-shui sin to ni?</td></tr><tr><td>18</td><td>The first who arrived was your brother</td><td>到先嗰個係你嘅兄弟</td><td>to sin ko-ko hai ni ke hing-tai</td></tr><tr><td>19</td><td>I heard he was the last who arrived</td><td>我聞得佢係至收尾到嘅</td><td>ngo măn tăk k&#x27;ü hai chi shau-mi to ke</td></tr></table>', '<table><tr><td>Headdress</td><td>首飾</td><td>shau''-shik</td><td>Petticoat</td><td>裙</td><td>kw''an</td></tr><tr><td>Nightcap</td><td>瞓帽</td><td>fün''mo''</td><td>Button</td><td>鈕</td><td>nau''</td></tr><tr><td>Pocket</td><td>衣袋</td><td>i-toi''</td><td>bag</td><td>袋</td><td>toi''</td></tr></table><tableborder="1"><tr><td>Apron</td><td>圍裙</td><td>wai-kw&#x27;an</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Thepeopleusehimill</td><td>個啲百姓刻薄待佢</td><td>ko-tipak-singhak-poktoik&#x27;ü</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Doeshecareforhisfriends?</td><td>佢顧住佢嘅朋友唔呢</td><td>k&#x27;üku-chük&#x27;ükep&#x27;ang-yau&#x27;mni?</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Heemptiedthewoodentub</td><td>佢倒清嗰個木桶</td><td>k&#x27;üto-ts&#x27;ingko-komuk-t&#x27;ung</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Tellhimtomixthemedicine</td><td>叫佢攪勻嗰啲藥</td><td>kiuk&#x27;ükau-wänko-tiyeuk</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Turntheboxupsidedown</td><td>倒轉個箱底向上</td><td>to-chünkoseungtaiheungsheung</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Turnthebaginsideout</td><td>翻轉個袋裏面出嚟</td><td>fan-chünkotoili-minch&#x27;utlai</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Don&#x27;tspoilthathat</td><td>咪整壞個頂帽</td><td>maiching-waikotingmo</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Putthemosquitonetoverthebed</td><td>擠個蚊袋在床上</td><td>chaikomăn-toitsoich&#x27;ong-sheung</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Allnationsuseclothes</td><td>萬國都用衣服嘅</td><td>man-kwoktoyungi-fukke</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Iamafraidthereisnohelpforit</td><td>我怕冇奈何咯</td><td>ngop&#x27;amo-noi-holok</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>Obligemebydoingthis</td><td>爲吓我做呢啲喇</td><td>waihangotsoni-tila</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>Menwearcoats,andwomenwearpetticoats</td><td>男人着長衫.女人着裙</td><td>nam-yancheukch&#x27;eung-sham,nü-yancheukkw&#x27;an<