27 They would not allow it to 佢哋唔肯俾佢洗 k''ü-ti ''m häng pi k''ü sai be washed

28 Do you understand the sentences given above?

上高所寫個啲句語你識得唔呢

sheung ko shoh se ko-ti kü ü n shik ták ''m ni?

29 They are not very clear 佢哋唔係十分明白 k''ü-ti ''m hai shap-fan mingpak

30 Chinese and English people 唐人共英國人唔係 T''ong-yan kung Ying-kwok yan are not quite alike 十分相同 ''m hai shap-fan seung t''ung

31 If you liked you might be 若係你中意.你或 yeuk hai ni chung-i, ni wak che taught 者可蒙教 ho mung kau

32 If we spoke Chinese daily we 若係我哋日日講 yeuk hai ngo-ti yat yat kong

should learn quickly 唐話就學得 T''ong-wa tsau hok tāk

快咯 fai lok

33 Are you quite sure of what 你所講嘅；你知得 ni shoh kong ke; ni chi tāk chān you said? 真唔呢 ''m ni?

34 I am sure of it; every body 我知得真咯；人人 ngo chi tāk chān lok; yan yan says so 都噉話 to kom wa

35 Excuse me! I think you are 恕我唔着喇,我估 sün ngo ''m cheuk la! ngo ku ni mistaken 你錯哩 ts''oh li

63 Permit me to say you are 容我講你唔着喇 yung ngo kong ni ''m cheuk wrong! la', '21Peoplesayheismuchtobe人哋話佢係十分可yan-tiwak''ühaishap-fanhopitied憐嘅linke22Heusesacorkscrewtoopen佢用個酒鑽嚟開嗰k''üyungkotsau-tsünlaihoithatbottle個樽ko-kotsun23Didyouputthetablecloth你放張檯布在檯上nifongcheungt''oi-potsoit''oionthetable?嚟咩sheunglaime?24Hashegetaladleanda佢有個壳共隻汁盅k''üyaukohokkungchekchap-gravydish?咩chungme?25Thatsmallknifeofhisisnot佢响張細刀仔唔值k''ükocheungsaito-tsai''mchikworthacash一個錢yatkots''in26Ifhewashedthebowlitwould若係佢洗過隻碗就yeukhaik''üsaikwochekuntsaubeclean乾淨嘅咯kon-tsingkelok27Theywouldnotallowitto佢哋唔肯俾佢洗k''ü-ti''mhängpik''üsaibewashed28Doyouunderstandthesentencesgivenabove?上高所寫個啲句語你識得唔呢sheungkoshohseko-tiküünshikták''mni?29Theyarenotveryclear佢哋唔係十分明白k''ü-ti''mhaishap-fanmingpak30ChineseandEnglishpeople唐人共英國人唔係T''ong-yankungYing-kwokyanarenotquitealike十分相同''mhaishap-fanseungt''ung31Ifyoulikedyoumightbe若係你中意.你或yeukhainichung-i,niwakchetaught者可蒙教homungkau32IfwespokeChinesedailywe若係我哋日日講yeukhaingo-tiyatyatkongshouldlearnquickly唐話就學得T''ong-watsauhoktāk快咯failok33Areyouquitesureofwhat你所講嘅；你知得nishohkongke;nichitākchānyousaid?真唔呢''mni?34Iamsureofit;everybody我知得真咯；人人ngochitākchānlok;yanyansaysso都噉話tokomwa35Excuseme!Ithinkyouare恕我唔着喇,我估sünngo''mcheukla!ngokunimistaken你錯哩ts''ohli63Permitmetosayyouare容我講你唔着喇yungngokongni''mcheukwrong!la', 'verified');

INSERT INTO articles (id, corpus, issue, issue_date, page, seq, title, text, text_norm, status) VALUES
  ('cvh-155-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 155, 1, NULL, '<table><tr><td>37 If the teacher says so, it can not be wrong</td><td>若係先生噉話就有錯嘅咯</td><td>yeuk hai sin shǎng kom wa tsau mo ts''oh ke lok</td></tr><tr><td>38 You may not hear rightly what he says</td><td>或者你聽唔眞佢話啫</td><td>wak che ni t''eng ''m chān k''ü wa che</td></tr><tr><td>39 If he speaks plainly we shall understand</td><td>若係佢講得明白我哋就識得咯</td><td>yeuk hai k''ü kong tāk ming-pak ngo-ti tsau shik tāk lok</td></tr><tr><td>40 Let us all commence today</td><td>等我哋喊嘭哈今日開工</td><td>tǎng ngo-ti ham-pang-lan kom-yat hoi kuug</td></tr></table>', '<table><tr><td>37Iftheteachersaysso,itcannotbewrong</td><td>若係先生噉話就有錯嘅咯</td><td>yeukhaisinshǎngkomwatsaumots''ohkelok</td></tr><tr><td>38Youmaynothearrightlywhathesays</td><td>或者你聽唔眞佢話啫</td><td>wakchenit''eng''mchānk''üwache</td></tr><tr><td>39Ifhespeaksplainlyweshallunderstand</td><td>若係佢講得明白我哋就識得咯</td><td>yeukhaik''ükongtākming-pakngo-titsaushiktāklok</td></tr><tr><td>40Letusallcommencetoday</td><td>等我哋喊嘭哈今日開工</td><td>tǎngngo-tiham-pang-lankom-yathoikuug</td></tr></table>', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-155-02', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 155, 2, 'LESSON XLVIII.', 'The following words are of frequent use with the conditional word.

<table><tr><td>Suppose that</td><td>倘若</td><td>t''ong''-yeuk</td><td>Unless</td><td>若唔係</td><td>yeuk ''m hai''</td></tr><tr><td>For instance</td><td>譬如</td><td>p''i''-ü</td><td>Do.</td><td>除非</td><td>ch''ü fi</td></tr><tr><td>Do.</td><td>設使</td><td>ch''it-sze''</td><td>Perhaps</td><td>或者</td><td>wak che''</td></tr><tr><td>Possibly</td><td>可以</td><td>ho''-i''</td><td>If</td><td>若係</td><td>yeuk hai''</td></tr><tr><td>Do.</td><td>能</td><td>nǎng</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table>', 'Thefollowingwordsareoffrequentusewiththeconditionalword.<table><tr><td>Supposethat</td><td>倘若</td><td>t''ong''-yeuk</td><td>Unless</td><td>若唔係</td><td>yeuk''mhai''</td></tr><tr><td>Forinstance</td><td>譬如</td><td>p''i''-ü</td><td>Do.</td><td>除非</td><td>ch''üfi</td></tr><tr><td>Do.</td><td>設使</td><td>ch''it-sze''</td><td>Perhaps</td><td>或者</td><td>wakche''</td></tr><tr><td>Possibly</td><td>可以</td><td>ho''-i''</td><td>If</td><td>若係</td><td>yeukhai''</td></tr><tr><td>Do.</td><td>能</td><td>nǎng</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table>', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-155-03', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 155, 3, 'ADVERBS OF PLACE.', 'Variations of the renderings given in former lessons will be found in the following list.

<table><tr><td>At what place?</td><td>乜地方</td><td>mǎt ti`-fong?</td><td>Far, far off</td><td>遠, 遠處</td><td>iän'', ün'' ch''ü</td></tr><tr><td>Do.</td><td>何處呢</td><td>ho ch''ü ni?</td><td>Near</td><td>近, 附近</td><td>kăn'', fu'' kăn''</td></tr><tr><td>Where?</td><td>邊吓呢</td><td>pin ha'' ni?</td><td>Ahroad</td><td>在外國</td><td>tsoi'' ngoi'' kwok</td></tr><tr><td>To the right</td><td>在右便</td><td>tsoi'' yau'' pin''</td><td>Outside</td><td>在外出</td><td>tsoi'' ngoi'' ch''ut</td></tr><tr><td>To the left</td><td>在左便</td><td>tsoi'' tsoh'' pin''</td><td>Hither</td><td>在呢處</td><td>tsoi'' ni ch''ü</td></tr><tr><td>Downwards</td><td>在下便</td><td>tsoi'' ha'' pin''</td><td>Whither</td><td>在响處</td><td>tsoi'' ko'' ch''ü</td></tr><tr><td>Backwards</td><td>背後便</td><td>pui'' hau'' pin''</td><td>Above</td><td>在上高</td><td>tsoi'' sheung'' ko</td></tr><tr><td>Behind</td><td>在後便</td><td>tsoi'' hau'' pin''</td><td>Below</td><td>在下底</td><td>tsoi'' ha'' tai</td></tr></table>', 'Variationsoftherenderingsgiveninformerlessonswillbefoundinthefollowinglist.<table><tr><td>Atwhatplace?</td><td>乜地方</td><td>mǎtti`-fong?</td><td>Far,faroff</td><td>遠,遠處</td><td>iän'',ün''ch''ü</td></tr><tr><td>Do.</td><td>何處呢</td><td>hoch''üni?</td><td>Near</td><td>近,附近</td><td>kăn'',fu''kăn''</td></tr><tr><td>Where?</td><td>邊吓呢</td><td>pinha''ni?</td><td>Ahroad</td><td>在外國</td><td>tsoi''ngoi''kwok</td></tr><tr><td>Totheright</td><td>在右便</td><td>tsoi''yau''pin''</td><td>Outside</td><td>在外出</td><td>tsoi''ngoi''ch''ut</td></tr><tr><td>Totheleft</td><td>在左便</td><td>tsoi''tsoh''pin''</td><td>Hither</td><td>在呢處</td><td>tsoi''nich''ü</td></tr><tr><td>Downwards</td><td>在下便</td><td>tsoi''ha''pin''</td><td>Whither</td><td>在响處</td><td>tsoi''ko''ch''ü</td></tr><tr><td>Backwards</td><td>背後便</td><td>pui''hau''pin''</td><td>Above</td><td>在上高</td><td>tsoi''sheung''ko</td></tr><tr><td>Behind</td><td>在後便</td><td>tsoi''hau''pin''</td><td>Below</td><td>在下底</td><td>tsoi''ha''tai</td></tr></table>', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-156-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 156, 1, NULL, '<table><tr><td>Aside</td><td>在一便</td><td>tsoi'' yut pin''</td><td>Round about</td><td>週圍</td><td>chau wai</td></tr><tr><td>Here</td><td>在呢便</td><td>tsoi'' ni pin''</td><td>Upwards</td><td>在上</td><td>tsoi'' sheung''</td></tr><tr><td>Do.</td><td>在呢處</td><td>tsoi'' ni ch''u''</td><td>Before</td><td>在前</td><td>tsoi'' ts''in</td></tr><tr><td>Yonder</td><td>在開頭</td><td>tsoi'' hoi t''au</td><td>There</td><td>响處</td><td>ko''-sh''ü''</td></tr></table>

<table><tr><td>You are very smart</td><td>你好底手嘅</td><td>ni'' ho'' tai shau'' ke''</td></tr><tr><td>To study (lit. read aloud) diligently</td><td>勤力讀書</td><td>k''ăn lik tuk shü</td></tr><tr><td>To exert oneself</td><td>出力做咯</td><td>ch''ut lik tso lok''</td></tr><tr><td>To shut both eyes</td><td>眯埋雙眼</td><td>mi mai sheung ngan''</td></tr><tr><td>Quite harmonious</td><td>一團和氣</td><td>yat t''ün woh hi''</td></tr><tr><td>Don''t worry me</td><td>咪厭悶我</td><td>mai''im mun'' ngo''</td></tr><tr><td>To sent a messenger</td><td>打發人去</td><td>ta''-fat yan hü''</td></tr><tr><td>Pour in a little more oil -</td><td>斟的油添</td><td>chǎm ti yau t''im</td></tr><tr><td>Pour out a little tea</td><td>斟的茶嚟</td><td>chǎm ti ch''a lai</td></tr><tr><td>So well dressed</td><td>咁好粧扮</td><td>kom'' ho'' chong-pan''</td></tr><tr><td>Dressed like a Chinese</td><td>扮唐人粧</td><td>pan'' T''ong-yan chong</td></tr><tr><td>He skipped a page (in reading)</td><td>嚬嘵一篇</td><td>lai hiu yat p''in</td></tr></table>

One advantage of the deficiencies (as Europeans are apt to consider them) of Chinese grammar, is that there is no such thing as an irregular verb, while nouns are "declined," if that term can be used, in a simple and unvarying way. This very simplicity, however, obliges rigid adherence to precise form in framing sentences, and the student will do well to commit every example given to memory.

<table><tr><td rowspan="2">Cheese (a bastard word)</td><td rowspan="2">之時餅</td><td>chi-shi-peng''</td><td>Teacup (large)</td><td>茶盅</td><td>ch''a-chung</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Table napkin</td><td>茶巾</td><td>ch''a-kun</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="2">Chicken pie</td><td rowspan="2">{鵰仔麵 龜</td><td>kai-tsai''-min-</td><td>Small waiter</td><td>茶盤</td><td>ch''a-p''un</td></tr><tr><td>kwai</td><td>Slop basin</td><td>茶碗</td><td>ch''a-un''</td></tr><tr><td>Tea board (waiter)</td><td>托盆</td><td>t''ok-p''un</td><td>Tea strainer</td><td>茶漏</td><td>ch''a-lau''</td></tr><tr><td>Chicken</td><td>{鵰仔</td><td>kai-tsai''</td><td>Tooth pick</td><td>牙簽</td><td>nga-ts''i-u</td></tr><tr><td>Capon</td><td>制鷄</td><td>sin''-kai</td><td>Soup ladle</td><td>湯壳</td><td>t''ong-hok</td></tr><tr><td>Crab</td><td>蟹</td><td>hai''</td><td>Table mat</td><td>碟墊</td><td>tip-tsin''</td></tr></table>

1 Where did you send the messenger to?

你打發個人去邊處呢

ni ta-fat ko yan hü pin-ch''ü ni?

2 Suppose that he does not return?

設使佢唔翻嚟呢

ch''it sze k''ü ''m fan lai ni?', '<table><tr><td>Aside</td><td>在一便</td><td>tsoi''yutpin''</td><td>Roundabout</td><td>週圍</td><td>chauwai</td></tr><tr><td>Here</td><td>在呢便</td><td>tsoi''nipin''</td><td>Upwards</td><td>在上</td><td>tsoi''sheung''</td></tr><tr><td>Do.</td><td>在呢處</td><td>tsoi''nich''u''</td><td>Before</td><td>在前</td><td>tsoi''ts''in</td></tr><tr><td>Yonder</td><td>在開頭</td><td>tsoi''hoit''au</td><td>There</td><td>响處</td><td>ko''-sh''ü''</td></tr></table><table><tr><td>Youareverysmart</td><td>你好底手嘅</td><td>ni''ho''taishau''ke''</td></tr><tr><td>Tostudy(lit.readaloud)diligently</td><td>勤力讀書</td><td>k''ănliktukshü</td></tr><tr><td>Toexertoneself</td><td>出力做咯</td><td>ch''utliktsolok''</td></tr><tr><td>Toshutbotheyes</td><td>眯埋雙眼</td><td>mimaisheungngan''</td></tr><tr><td>Quiteharmonious</td><td>一團和氣</td><td>yatt''ünwohhi''</td></tr><tr><td>Don''tworryme</td><td>咪厭悶我</td><td>mai''immun''ngo''</td></tr><tr><td>Tosentamessenger</td><td>打發人去</td><td>ta''-fatyanhü''</td></tr><tr><td>Pourinalittlemoreoil-</td><td>斟的油添</td><td>chǎmtiyaut''im</td></tr><tr><td>Pouroutalittletea</td><td>斟的茶嚟</td><td>chǎmtich''alai</td></tr><tr><td>Sowelldressed</td><td>咁好粧扮</td><td>kom''ho''chong-pan''</td></tr><tr><td>DressedlikeaChinese</td><td>扮唐人粧</td><td>pan''T''ong-yanchong</td></tr><tr><td>Heskippedapage(inreading)</td><td>嚬嘵一篇</td><td>laihiuyatp''in</td></tr></table>Oneadvantageofthedeficiencies(asEuropeansareapttoconsiderthem)ofChinesegrammar,isthatthereisnosuchthingasanirregularverb,whilenounsare"declined,"ifthattermcanbeused,inasimpleandunvaryingway.Thisverysimplicity,however,obligesrigidadherencetopreciseforminframingsentences,andthestudentwilldowelltocommiteveryexamplegiventomemory.<table><tr><tdrowspan="2">Cheese(abastardword)</td><tdrowspan="2">之時餅</td><td>chi-shi-peng''</td><td>Teacup(large)</td><td>茶盅</td><td>ch''a-chung</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Tablenapkin</td><td>茶巾</td><td>ch''a-kun</td></tr><tr><tdrowspan="2">Chickenpie</td><tdrowspan="2">{鵰仔麵龜</td><td>kai-tsai''-min-</td><td>Smallwaiter</td><td>茶盤</td><td>ch''a-p''un</td></tr><tr><td>kwai</td><td>Slopbasin</td><td>茶碗</td><td>ch''a-un''</td></tr><tr><td>Teaboard(waiter)</td><td>托盆</td><td>t''ok-p''un</td><td>Teastrainer</td><td>茶漏</td><td>ch''a-lau''</td></tr><tr><td>Chicken</td><td>{鵰仔</td><td>kai-tsai''</td><td>Toothpick</td><td>牙簽</td><td>nga-ts''i-u</td></tr><tr><td>Capon</td><td>制鷄</td><td>sin''-kai</td><td>Soupladle</td><td>湯壳</td><td>t''ong-hok</td></tr><tr><td>Crab</td><td>蟹</td><td>hai''</td><td>Tablemat</td><td>碟墊</td><td>tip-tsin''</td></tr></table>1Wheredidyousendthemessengerto?你打發個人去邊處呢nita-fatkoyanhüpin-ch''üni?2Supposethathedoesnotreturn?設使佢唔翻嚟呢ch''itszek''ü''mfanlaini?', 'verified'),
  ('cvh-157-01', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', 'canton-vernacular-handbook', '1874', 157, 1, NULL, '<table><tr><td>3 Perhaps, he will not exert himself</td><td>或者佢唔肯出力</td><td>wak che k''ü ''m hǎng ch''ut lik</td></tr><tr><td>4 Unless he studies diligently he will be punished</td><td>若唔係佢勤力讀書,佢就受責罰咯</td><td>yeuk ''m hai k''ü k''ăn-lik tuk shü, k''ü tsau shau chăk-fat lok</td></tr><tr><td>5 How can he possibly study? he has no time</td><td>佢點能讀書啫佢有 時候哩</td><td>k''ü tim nǎng tuk shü che? k''ü mo shi-hau li</td></tr><tr><td>6 Tell me, for intance, if he is lazy</td><td>話我知,譬如佢懶惰啞</td><td>wa ngo chi, p''i-ü k''ü lan-to a</td></tr><tr><td>7 At what place is his house?</td><td>佢嘅屋在邊處呢</td><td>k''ü ke uk tsoi pin ch''ü ni?</td></tr><tr><td>8 First turn to the right, and then to the left</td><td>先轉過右,後轉過左</td><td>sin chün kwo yau, hau chün kwo tsoh</td></tr><tr><td>9 Walk round about the town</td><td>响個城週圍行過咯</td><td>ko-ko shing chau-wai hang kwo lok</td></tr><tr><td>10 Is that a man or a boy yonder?</td><td>在開頭處响個係大人只細文仔呢</td><td>tsoi-hoi-t''au ch''ü ko-ko hai tai yan chi sai-mău-tsai ni?</td></tr><tr><td>11 I can''t see; it is too far off</td><td>我睇唔見;遠得嚌</td><td>ngo t''ai''m kin; ün tāk tsai</td></tr><tr><td>12 Does he live above or below the road?</td><td>佢在路上只路下居住呢</td><td>k''ü tsoi lo sheung chi lo ha kü chü ni?</td></tr><tr><td>13 He lives behind the barracks</td><td>佢在兵房後便住</td><td>k''ü tsoi ping-fong hau pin chü</td></tr><tr><td>14 Has your father ever been abroad?</td><td>你令尊有出過外有呢</td><td>ni ling-tsün yau ch''ut kwo ngoi mo ni?</td></tr><tr><td>15 Smoke goes upwards; water flows downwards</td><td>烟從上去;水望下流</td><td>in ts''ung sheung hü; shui mong ha lau</td></tr><tr><td>16 Had you ever seen him before?</td><td>你從前有見過佢有呢</td><td>ni ts''ung ts''in yau kin kwo k''ü mo ni?</td></tr><tr><td>17 Possibly I have seen him once</td><td>或者我有見過佢都未定</td><td>wak che ngo yau kin kwo k''ü to mi ting</td></tr><tr><td>18 Put the table mat on the table</td><td>放塊檯墊在張檯面嚟</td><td>fong fai t''oi-ts''in tsoi cheung t''oi min lai</td></tr><tr><td>19 Take care not to break the soup ladle</td><td>子細咪打爛個隻湯壳</td><td>tsz-sai mai ta-lan ko chek t''ong hok</td></tr><tr><td>20 Bring the cups here on a tea-board</td><td>俾個托盆拈啲杯嚟呢處</td><td>pi ko t''ok-p''un nim ti pui lai ni-ch''ü</td></tr><tr><td>21 Pour the tea into the slop basin</td><td>倒啲茶落個茶碗嚟</td><td>to ti ch''a lok ko ch''a-un lai</td></tr></table>

22 What is the use of a tooth-pick? 牙簽做乜用嘅呢 nga-ts''im tso măt yung ke ni?', '<table><tr><td>3Perhaps,hewillnotexerthimself</td><td>或者佢唔肯出力</td><td>wakchek''ü''mhǎngch''utlik</td></tr><tr><td>4Unlesshestudiesdiligentlyhewillbepunished</td><td>若唔係佢勤力讀書,佢就受責罰咯</td><td>yeuk''mhaik''ük''ăn-liktukshü,k''ütsaushauchăk-fatlok</td></tr><tr><td>5Howcanhepossiblystudy?hehasnotime</td><td>佢點能讀書啫佢有時候哩</td><td>k''ütimnǎngtukshüche?k''ümoshi-hauli</td></tr><tr><td>6Tellme,forintance,ifheislazy</td><td>話我知,譬如佢懶惰啞</td><td>wangochi,p''i-ük''ülan-toa</td></tr><tr><td>7Atwhatplaceishishouse?</td><td>佢嘅屋在邊處呢</td><td>k''ükeuktsoipinch''üni?</td></tr><tr><td>8Firstturntotheright,andthentotheleft</td><td>先轉過右,後轉過左</td><td>sinchünkwoyau,hauchünkwotsoh</td></tr><tr><td>9Walkroundaboutthetown</td><td>响個城週圍行過咯</td><td>ko-koshingchau-waihangkwolok</td></tr><tr><td>10Isthatamanoraboyyonder?</td><td>在開頭處响個係大人只細文仔呢</td><td>tsoi-hoi-t''auch''üko-kohaitaiyanchisai-mău-tsaini?</td></tr><tr><td>11Ican''tsee;itistoofaroff</td><td>我睇唔見;遠得嚌</td><td>ngot''ai''mkin;üntāktsai</td></tr><tr><td>12Doesheliveaboveorbelowtheroad?</td><td>佢在路上只路下居住呢</td><td>k''ütsoilosheungchilohaküchüni?</td></tr><tr><td>13Helivesbehindthebarracks</td><td>佢在兵房後便住</td><td>k''ütsoiping-fonghaupinchü</td></tr><tr><td>14Hasyourfathereverbeenabroad?</td><td>你令尊有出過外有呢</td><td>niling-tsünyauch''utkwongoimoni?</td></tr><tr><td>15Smokegoesupwards;waterflowsdownwards</td><td>烟從上去;水望下流</td><td>ints''ungsheunghü;shuimonghalau</td></tr><tr><td>16Hadyoueverseenhimbefore?</td><td>你從前有見過佢有呢</td><td>nits''ungts''inyaukinkwok''ümoni?</td></tr><tr><td>17PossiblyIhaveseenhimonce</td><td>或者我有見過佢都未定</td><td>wakchengoyaukinkwok''ütomiting</td></tr><tr><td>18Putthetablematonthetable</td><td>放塊檯墊在張檯面嚟</td><td>fongfait''oi-ts''intsoicheungt''oiminlai</td></tr><tr><td>19Takecarenottobreakthesoupladle</td><td>子細咪打爛個隻湯壳</td><td>tsz-saimaita-lankochekt''onghok</td></tr><tr><td>20Bringthecupshereonatea-board</td><td>俾個托盆拈啲杯嚟呢處</td><td>pikot''ok-p''unnimtipuilaini-ch''ü</td></tr><tr><td>21Pourtheteaintotheslopbasin</td><td>倒啲茶落個茶碗嚟</td><td>totich''alokkoch''a-unlai</td></tr></table>22Whatistheuseofatooth-pick?牙簽做乜用嘅呢nga-ts''imtsomătyungkeni?', 'verified'),
