  ('rcc-050-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 50, 1, 'LESSON, IV.', 'This large place we live in is called the world. It is very beautiful. If we look up we see the blue sky, if we look down we see the green grass.

The sky is like a curtain spread over our heads, the grass like a carpet under our feet, and the bright sun is like a candle to give us light.—''Peep of Day,'' p. 37.

我哋而家所住嘅地方，就叫做世界，真係好睇嘅咯。担高頭，你見有個天，垂抵頭，又見地上嘅青草。

天係好似一張大布帳，地上嘅青草好似一張大蓆，個熱頭好似一盞大燈，等我哋光猛睇得見野。', 'Thislargeplaceweliveiniscalledtheworld.Itisverybeautiful.Ifwelookupweseethebluesky,ifwelookdownweseethegreengrass.Theskyislikeacurtainspreadoverourheads,thegrasslikeacarpetunderourfeet,andthebrightsunislikeacandletogiveuslight.—''PeepofDay,''p.37.我哋而家所住嘅地方，就叫做世界，真係好睇嘅咯。担高頭，你見有個天，垂抵頭，又見地上嘅青草。天係好似一張大布帳，地上嘅青草好似一張大蓆，個熱頭好似一盞大燈，等我哋光猛睇得見野。', 'needs_review'),
  ('rcc-050-02', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 50, 2, 'LESSON, V.', 'When God made the dry land, there was nothing on it: it was bare. So God spake, and things grew out of the ground. Trees came out of it; they were covered with green leaves of different shapes. Some were called oak-trees, and some were called elm trees, and some beech-trees. And some trees bore nice fruit, such as plum-trees, apple-trees, orange-trees, and fig-trees.—''Peep of Day,'' p. 41.

上帝已經造起旱地，個陣時，各樣物件未曾有得生出，上帝又話，各樣嘅物，要喺地上生出嚟，噉就有樹木生出咯，個啲樹葉各有唔同嘅，有啲叫做榕樹，有啲叫做松樹，有啲叫做竹樹之類。又有好多樹會生出果嘅，有啲生桃，有啲生荔枝，有啲生沙梨，有啲生柑橙之類。', 'WhenGodmadethedryland,therewasnothingonit:itwasbare.SoGodspake,andthingsgrewoutoftheground.Treescameoutofit;theywerecoveredwithgreenleavesofdifferentshapes.Somewerecalledoak-trees,andsomewerecalledelmtrees,andsomebeech-trees.Andsometreesborenicefruit,suchasplum-trees,apple-trees,orange-trees,andfig-trees.—''PeepofDay,''p.41.上帝已經造起旱地，個陣時，各樣物件未曾有得生出，上帝又話，各樣嘅物，要喺地上生出嚟，噉就有樹木生出咯，個啲樹葉各有唔同嘅，有啲叫做榕樹，有啲叫做松樹，有啲叫做竹樹之類。又有好多樹會生出果嘅，有啲生桃，有啲生荔枝，有啲生沙梨，有啲生柑橙之類。', 'needs_review'),
