  ('rcc-057-02', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 57, 2, 'LESSON, IX.', 'Ye- sò tsoi² shai¹ chi shi, shi-shong kei'' -nim² k''öü ke''t''in fu², ho chung-yi'' tuk₂ tsz² -kéi hai shu'' k''éi-''t''o Shöng²-taí'', yau shi k''öü k''éi-''t''o ngán-lui² lau tak'' ho tsai-long.

Jesus in world''s time constantly remembered thought of his Heavenly Father much liked alone (by) himself at place prayed God, have times he prayed tears flowed very bitterly.', 'Ye-sòtsoi²shai¹chishi,shi-shongkei''-nim²k''öüke''t''infu²,hochung-yi''tuk₂tsz²-kéihaishu''k''éi-''t''oShöng²-taí'',yaushik''öük''éi-''t''ongán-lui²lautak''hotsai-long.Jesusinworld''stimeconstantlyrememberedthoughtofhisHeavenlyFathermuchlikedalone(by)himselfatplaceprayedGod,havetimesheprayedtearsflowedverybitterly.', 'verified'),
  ('rcc-058-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 58, 1, NULL, 'One night Jesus prayed all night alone upon the top of a high hill.

Sometimes Jesus prayed to his Father while his disciples stood near and listened.

Once when Jesus had been praying with them they said, ''Teach us to pray.'' Then Jesus taught them a little prayer.

It was this: ''Our Father which art in heaven, hallowed be thy name. Thy kingdom come. Thy will he done in earth, as it is in heaven. Give us this day our daily bread. And forgive us our trespasses as we forgive them that trespass against us. And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil: for thine is the kingdom, and the power, and the glory, for ever and ever. Amen.''— ''Peep of Day,'' pp. 110,112.

又有時成夜喺山頂祈禱。

佢拜天父時,門徒常有企側便嚟聽。

有日門徒求佢話,主呀,教我哋祈禱吖,耶穌就拈呢章祈禱文嚟教佢。

吾父在天,願爾之名尊為至聖,願爾之國降臨於世,願爾旨意得成,在地猶如在天,所用之糧,今日賜我,求免我負,如我免人之負,使我不入試惑,救我出惡,因國,與權,與榮,皆爾所有,至到世世代代,誠心所願。', 'OnenightJesusprayedallnightaloneuponthetopofahighhill.SometimesJesusprayedtohisFatherwhilehisdisciplesstoodnearandlistened.OncewhenJesushadbeenprayingwiththemtheysaid,''Teachustopray.''ThenJesustaughtthemalittleprayer.Itwasthis:''OurFatherwhichartinheaven,hallowedbethyname.Thykingdomcome.Thywillhedoneinearth,asitisinheaven.Giveusthisdayourdailybread.Andforgiveusourtrespassesasweforgivethemthattrespassagainstus.Andleadusnotintotemptation,butdeliverusfromevil:forthineisthekingdom,andthepower,andtheglory,foreverandever.Amen.''—''PeepofDay,''pp.110,112.又有時成夜喺山頂祈禱。佢拜天父時,門徒常有企側便嚟聽。有日門徒求佢話,主呀,教我哋祈禱吖,耶穌就拈呢章祈禱文嚟教佢。吾父在天,願爾之名尊為至聖,願爾之國降臨於世,願爾旨意得成,在地猶如在天,所用之糧,今日賜我,求免我負,如我免人之負,使我不入試惑,救我出惡,因國,與權,與榮,皆爾所有,至到世世代代,誠心所願。', 'needs_review'),
  ('rcc-058-02', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 58, 2, 'LESSON X.', 'One morning very early, when Jesus had been dead only two days, the poor women came into the garden. It was not quite light yet; for the sun was just rising.

耶穌已經死曉兩日,到第三朝天光時,個啲敬愛耶穌嘅女人,帶齊香膏香料,想去花園。', 'Onemorningveryearly,whenJesushadbeendeadonlytwodays,thepoorwomencameintothegarden.Itwasnotquitelightyet;forthesunwasjustrising.耶穌已經死曉兩日,到第三朝天光時,個啲敬愛耶穌嘅女人,帶齊香膏香料,想去花園。', 'needs_review'),
  ('rcc-059-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 59, 1, NULL, 'Yau² yau shi sheng† ye² hai shan

