  ('rcc-062-02', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 62, 2, 'LESSON, XI.', 'Compare the feelings of others by your own.

If you do not like any thing yourself, do not give it to others.

By acting in this way, your steps will tread the right road.

Observe the rules do not rebel against the Lord.

I would not wish anyone to steal my things.

Other people have the same feelings.

I would not like to be struck.

Other people feel the same.

If I am in trouble, I wish people to help me.

If I see any one else in trouble, I ought to render my help.

By acting in this way, you will be able to escape calamities.

Whether at home or abroad.—''The Four Character Book.''

