  ('rcc-070-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 70, 1, NULL, 'Jacob had twelve sons. * * * Joseph was only seventeen years old and Benjamin was but a small child. All the others were grown up. The ten brothers were very bad: they had no fear of God in their hearts at all. Joseph was not like this: he really loved God. Jacob loved Joseph most of all his sons and made him a coat of many colours for him to wear. When his ten brothers saw that their Father loved Joseph, they hated him, and always oppressed him. God loved Joseph and always took care of him. One night Joseph dreamed he was in the field with his brother binding up sheaves of corn; and his brothers'' sheaves all bowed down before his sheaf. God told Joseph what this meant.

It meant that Joseph''s brothers at some future time would serve Joseph. His brothers were very angry with Joseph when they heard him say so. Before very long Joseph had another dream.

雅各十二個仔,* * * 個陣時約瑟十七歲大咁,便雅憫就有幾大個,其餘十個都長大咯,但十兄弟十分惡嘅,有啲敬畏神嘅心,約瑟就唔係噉,實首愛神,雅各至愛佢,整件花衫佢着,個啲兄弟見父親噉,就好憎約瑟,時時蝦佢,神就好愛約瑟,時時保佑佢,有一晚約瑟夢見自己喺田處,共埋兄弟束起的禾把,束起個時,個啲兄弟嘅把把都仆倒地處,拜約瑟所束個一把,呢啲意思,係神特登令約瑟知。

後來佢兄弟是必服約瑟。兄弟聽見約瑟噉樣子,好嬲約瑟,過曉冇耐,佢又試發夢。', 'Jacobhadtwelvesons.***JosephwasonlyseventeenyearsoldandBenjaminwasbutasmallchild.Alltheothersweregrownup.Thetenbrotherswereverybad:theyhadnofearofGodintheirheartsatall.Josephwasnotlikethis:hereallylovedGod.JacoblovedJosephmostofallhissonsandmadehimacoatofmanycoloursforhimtowear.WhenhistenbrotherssawthattheirFatherlovedJoseph,theyhatedhim,andalwaysoppressedhim.GodlovedJosephandalwaystookcareofhim.OnenightJosephdreamedhewasinthefieldwithhisbrotherbindingupsheavesofcorn;andhisbrothers''sheavesallboweddownbeforehissheaf.GodtoldJosephwhatthismeant.ItmeantthatJoseph''sbrothersatsomefuturetimewouldserveJoseph.HisbrotherswereveryangrywithJosephwhentheyheardhimsayso.BeforeverylongJosephhadanotherdream.雅各十二個仔,***個陣時約瑟十七歲大咁,便雅憫就有幾大個,其餘十個都長大咯,但十兄弟十分惡嘅,有啲敬畏神嘅心,約瑟就唔係噉,實首愛神,雅各至愛佢,整件花衫佢着,個啲兄弟見父親噉,就好憎約瑟,時時蝦佢,神就好愛約瑟,時時保佑佢,有一晚約瑟夢見自己喺田處,共埋兄弟束起的禾把,束起個時,個啲兄弟嘅把把都仆倒地處,拜約瑟所束個一把,呢啲意思,係神特登令約瑟知。後來佢兄弟是必服約瑟。兄弟聽見約瑟噉樣子,好嬲約瑟,過曉冇耐,佢又試發夢。', 'needs_review'),
  ('rcc-071-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 71, 1, 'LESSON, XIV.', 'Ngá-kok, yau shap₂-yi₂ ko'' tsai.

* * * Ko'' chan₂ shi Yök₂-shat, shap₂-ts''at, sui'' tái₂ chek, Pin²-ngá-man tsau₂ mo ''kei tái₂ ko''. K''éi-yü ko'' ko'' to chöng-tái₂ lok. K''öü shap₂ hing-tai² shap₂-fan ok, ke'': mò ti king-wai Shan ke'' sam. Yök₂-shat, tsau² m hai₂ ''kòm: k''öü shat₂-shau oi Shan. Ngá-kok ch''oí oi k''öü, ching kin₂ fá sham k''öü chök. Ko'' shap₂ hing-tai₂ kin'' fú₂-ts''an kòm, tsau₂ hó tsang Yök₂-shat, shi-shi há k''öü. Shan tsau₂ hò oi Yök₂-shat, shi-shi pó-yau² k''öü. Yau yat, mán Yök₂-shat, mung² kín¹ tsz₂-kéi hai₂ t''in shü'', kung²-mai hing-tai₂ ch''uk, hei ti wo pa; ch''uk, hei ko'' shi, ko''-ti hing-tai₂ ke'', pá-pa to p''uk, to téi₂ shu'' pai Yök₂-shat, sho ch''uk, ko'' yat, pá. Ni-ti yi''-sz hai₂ Shan tak₂-tang ling₂ Yök₂-shat, chi.

Hau²-loi k''öü hing-tai² shi²-pit, fuk₂ Yök₂-shat. Hing-tai² t''eng† kín³ Yök₂-shat, kòm yong²-tsz hó nau Yök₂-shat. Kwo³ hiú mò noi* k''öü yau² shi³ fát₀-mung².

Jacob had twelve [C.] sons. * * *

That period time Joseph seventeen years big only 7, Benjamin, just not much big [C.] Remainder each [C.] also grown-up 32. They ten brothers ten parts bad: not (even a) little reverence and fear God (kind of) heart. Joseph just not was so, he really loved God. Jacob most loved him, made him flowery jacket (for) him to wear. Those ten brothers seeing (their) father so, then much hated Joseph, constantly bullied him. God just much loved Joseph, always protected him. There-was one night Joseph dreamt (he) saw himself in field place together with (his) brothers binding up the paddy sheaves; binding up that time those brother''s (ones) sheaf sheaf even prostrated to (the) ground place and did reverence (to) Joseph what binded that one sheaf. These meanings had God determinately caused Joseph to know.

