  ('rcc-078-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 78, 1, NULL, 'He went quickly to his brothers and said, ''The child is not here. I do not know what to do.'' The brothers paid no attention to him. They killed a kid at once, and taking Joseph''s coat of many colours they dipped it into the blood of the kid, and took it home to show to their father. They said, ''Is this coat which we have found Joseph''s?'' As soon as Jacob saw it, he said, ''It is his. A wild beast has eaten him, my son Joseph is not.''

急啲去對兄弟話,個細蚊仔唔喺處咯,我唔知點算,個啲兄弟總唔睬佢,即時重劏一隻羊仔,將約瑟個件花衫浸落羊血處,拎去歸俾過父親睇,話,呢件衫係我哋搵倒嘅,係約瑟嘅衫唔係,雅各一見就認得個件衫話,冇錯,係佢嘅咯,必定被一隻野獸食死佢,我個仔約瑟必定冇曉咯。

Jacob had deceived his father, and now his children were deceiving him. * * *.

本來雅各已經呃自己父親,而家仔又呃佢。* * *

Jacob thought that his son was really dead and he was very sad; he wept aloud, tore his clothes, and would not be comforted.—''Bible History for the Least and Lowest.''

雅各個時估個仔眞正死喇,佢個心就好閉翳咯,大聲喊,掹爛自己衫,又唔受人安慰。', 'Hewentquicklytohisbrothersandsaid,''Thechildisnothere.Idonotknowwhattodo.''Thebrotherspaidnoattentiontohim.Theykilledakidatonce,andtakingJoseph''scoatofmanycolourstheydippeditintothebloodofthekid,andtookithometoshowtotheirfather.Theysaid,''IsthiscoatwhichwehavefoundJoseph''s?''AssoonasJacobsawit,hesaid,''Itishis.Awildbeasthaseatenhim,mysonJosephisnot.''急啲去對兄弟話,個細蚊仔唔喺處咯,我唔知點算,個啲兄弟總唔睬佢,即時重劏一隻羊仔,將約瑟個件花衫浸落羊血處,拎去歸俾過父親睇,話,呢件衫係我哋搵倒嘅,係約瑟嘅衫唔係,雅各一見就認得個件衫話,冇錯,係佢嘅咯,必定被一隻野獸食死佢,我個仔約瑟必定冇曉咯。Jacobhaddeceivedhisfather,andnowhischildrenweredeceivinghim.***.本來雅各已經呃自己父親,而家仔又呃佢。***Jacobthoughtthathissonwasreallydeadandhewasverysad;heweptaloud,torehisclothes,andwouldnotbecomforted.—''BibleHistoryfortheLeastandLowest.''雅各個時估個仔眞正死喇,佢個心就好閉翳咯,大聲喊,掹爛自己衫,又唔受人安慰。', 'needs_review'),
