The men then said, ''From Jerusalem brought to-come (here) that Daniel not obey your decree, one day''s course also three times pray-to God.''', 'Kòmk''öüfún-''héimín²hög''kopín²laípai''.K''öüyat²-yat²sámchòng''tóhaï²kòmkwai²-tòkoshü''laípai''Shan,to-tse²Shankòmtái²yan-tín,toi²k''öü.Yi-kách''ut,hiúko''ming²-ling'',k''öütohai²chiúyat,yöng''kòmpai''Sohewas-pleased(tohavehis)facetowardsthatsidein-order-topray.Heday(by)daythreetimesalsodidsokneel-atthatplacein-order-toprayto-Godto-thankGodsuchgreatgracetowardshim.Nowissuedhadthedecree,healsodidaccording-toonesamesopray.Ko''-titsangTán²-yi-léike''yant''eng†-mank''öüchiú''kan²kòmpai'':k''öü-tei²yat,yat,chí-to''hai²k''öüpai''-ke''shí-hau²tsau²huí''chongk''öü,tangk''öü-tei²tsò-takwá''ko''wongchi,haí²k''öü-tei²ts''anngánkin''k''öüpai''Those(who)hatedDanielpeopleheardheaccording-toold(time)soprayed:theyonedayknewit-washisprayingtimethenwentto-spy-onhimso-thattheydocouldsay-totheKingto-knowitwastheywith-their-ownedeyessawhimpray.K''öü-tei²tsan²laítuì''ko''wongwá'',Néimhaï²ch''ut,hiúyat,ko''ming²-ling'',wák''-cheyat,ko''yansám-shap²yat,kòmnoi²,yaupai''Shan,mhaï²tukpai''néi,tsan²yiu''wingk''öülok''sz-tau''Theythencame(and)totheKingsaid,''Younothave(i.e.Haveyounot)issueddonea[C.]decree(totheeffectthat),ifa[C.]man(forthespaceof)thirtydayssolongdidprayto-God,(and)notdidonlyprayto-you,thenmustthrowndownlions''den?''Ko''wongwá'',Hai²''chanke''lok,ngoyau''mkoitak,ni-co''ming²-ling''ke''TheKingsaid,''Itistrue,32,Ialsonotchangeablethisdecree.''Ko''-tiyantsau²wá'',HaiYe-lo²-sát.-lángtái''laiko''Tán²-yi-léimt''eng†néi-ke''ming²-ling'',yat,yat,chikántosámp''inpai''Shan.''Thementhensaid,''FromJerusalembroughtto-come(here)thatDanielnotobeyyourdecree,oneday''scoursealsothreetimespray-toGod.''', 'verified'),
  ('rcc-086-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 86, 1, NULL, 'Then the King was very sorry that he had made a law against praying, and tried to think of some way of not letting Daniel be killed.

個王個時就好閉翳咯,就想揾法子嚟救個但以理,等佢唔使俾個啲獅咬死。

But he could think of no way. In the evening the men came to him and said, ''You cannot alter the law that you have made, for in our country it is a law that laws may not be altered.''

但冇法子,到挨晚個啲人嚟對個王話,你唔得改變你個啲命令,因呢個國出過命令,是必唔改得嘅咯。

Then the King desired Daniel to be brought, and he was cast into a den of lions; the lions lived in a deep place underground. Lions are always very hungry in the evening, and roar for their food. Would they not eat up Daniel as soon as he was thrown into the den?

個王就吩咐人帶但以理嚟採落獅竇處,個啲獅係困落一個大竉,到挨晚佢時時都好肚餓嘅。

But Darius knew that Daniel''s God was a very great God, and he said to Daniel, ''Your God whom you serve always, is able to deliver you.''

大利烏知到但以理所拜個位神,係好尊大嘅,佢就對但以理話,你時時所服事嘅神,有能救你嘅。

I think Darius must have heard how God once saved three men from being burnt in the furnace.

大概大利烏聽聞人講過,神先日救過三個人出曉火爐。

A stone was brought, and laid upon the top of the den.

