  ('rcc-098-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 98, 1, 'LESSON, XVII.', 'How delightful is the description the Bible gives of heaven. We are told that sickness, sorrow, and death never enter there; that cares, fears, and anxieties are never felt there; that poverty, privation, unkindness, and disappointment are never known there. The body that will rise from the grave will be ''incorruptible,'' and will never experience pain, weariness, or decay. Old age will never enfeeble, for there will be perpetual youth; and death will never snatch away those we love, for death itself will be destroyed. What is still better, there will be no more sin, but all hearts will be full of holy love to God, and to one another. Every one will rejoice in the society and happiness of every one else, and God himself will dwell among them. All the good men of former ages will be there—the martyrs, and apostles, and prophets. There, too, we shall meet with angels and arch-angels; and more then all, we shall behold Jesus in his glorified human body—we shall see his face, and ever be with the Lord.

聖書所講喺天堂處十分好，冇病痛冇閉翳，冇艱難冇貧窮唔會死，唔使掛慮，唔使驚慌，唔怕人待你唔好，事事從心所欲日久不變，長生不老。其中至好嘅，係罪惡脫甩晒，好熱心愛眞神愛人，大家長長歡喜。一則歡喜見耶穌嘅面，時時同埋佢住。二則歡喜自己冇罪惡。三則歡喜古時善人，衆天使喺處，一齊讚美眞神。', 'HowdelightfulisthedescriptiontheBiblegivesofheaven.Wearetoldthatsickness,sorrow,anddeathneverenterthere;thatcares,fears,andanxietiesareneverfeltthere;thatpoverty,privation,unkindness,anddisappointmentareneverknownthere.Thebodythatwillrisefromthegravewillbe''incorruptible,''andwillneverexperiencepain,weariness,ordecay.Oldagewillneverenfeeble,fortherewillbeperpetualyouth;anddeathwillneversnatchawaythosewelove,fordeathitselfwillbedestroyed.Whatisstillbetter,therewillbenomoresin,butallheartswillbefullofholylovetoGod,andtooneanother.Everyonewillrejoiceinthesocietyandhappinessofeveryoneelse,andGodhimselfwilldwellamongthem.Allthegoodmenofformerageswillbethere—themartyrs,andapostles,andprophets.There,too,weshallmeetwithangelsandarch-angels;andmorethenall,weshallbeholdJesusinhisglorifiedhumanbody—weshallseehisface,andeverbewiththeLord.聖書所講喺天堂處十分好，冇病痛冇閉翳，冇艱難冇貧窮唔會死，唔使掛慮，唔使驚慌，唔怕人待你唔好，事事從心所欲日久不變，長生不老。其中至好嘅，係罪惡脫甩晒，好熱心愛眞神愛人，大家長長歡喜。一則歡喜見耶穌嘅面，時時同埋佢住。二則歡喜自己冇罪惡。三則歡喜古時善人，衆天使喺處，一齊讚美眞神。', 'needs_review'),
  ('rcc-099-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 99, 1, 'LESSON, XVII.', 'Shing''- shü ''sho ''kong ''hai t''in-''tong shü'', shap²-fan ''hò: mò peng²-tung''; mò pai-ai''; mò kán-nán; mò p''an-k''ung; m wui sz, m shai kwá-lui²; m shaí king-fong; m p''a yan toi² nei m hò, sz²-sz ts''ung sam ''sho yuk²; yat² kan pat, pin''; ch''ong sháng pat, lo; K''ei chung chi ''hô ke'', hai² tsui²-ok t''tut lat sai'', ho yit² sam oi chan Shan oi yan, tai²-kä ch''ong ch''ong fün-hei. Yat tsak: fün-hei kin Ye-so ke min², shi-shi t''ung mai k''öü chü''. Yi² tsak: fün-hei tsz²-kéi mò tsui²-ok. Sám tsak: fún-hei kwú shi² shin² yan, chung t''in-sz hai shu'': yat ts''ai tsán-méi chan Shan.

Holy book (according-to) what (it) says, (there is) at heaven''s place ten parts good, no illness, no sorrow, no trouble, no poverty, not able to die, not need anxious-caring-for (matters), not need to-be-frightened, no fear peopleact-towards you not well. Thing thing (i.e. every thing) according-to. heart what like. Days long not change, long life not old. Their midst most good is sin evil take off altogether, very hot heart love true God, love man. All long long happy. First place: happy see Jesus''s face, always together with him live. Secondly: happy self not have sin, evil. Thirdly: happy (because) ancient times good men, all angels at place: one altogether praise true God.', 'Shing''-shü''sho''kong''hait''in-''tongshü'',shap²-fan''hò:mòpeng²-tung'';mòpai-ai'';mòkán-nán;mòp''an-k''ung;mwuisz,mshaikwá-lui²;mshaíking-fong;mp''ayantoi²neimhò,sz²-szts''ungsam''shoyuk²;yat²kanpat,pin'';ch''ongshángpat,lo;K''eichungchi''hôke'',hai²tsui²-okt''tutlatsai'',hoyit²samoichanShanoiyan,tai²-käch''ongch''ongfün-hei.Yattsak:fün-heikinYe-sokemin²,shi-shit''ungmaik''öüchü''.Yi²tsak:fün-heitsz²-kéimòtsui²-ok.Sámtsak:fún-heikwúshi²shin²yan,chungt''in-szhaishu'':yatts''aitsán-méichanShan.Holybook(according-to)what(it)says,(thereis)atheaven''splacetenpartsgood,noillness,nosorrow,notrouble,nopoverty,notabletodie,notneedanxious-caring-for(matters),notneedto-be-frightened,nofearpeopleact-towardsyounotwell.Thingthing(i.e.everything)according-to.heartwhatlike.Dayslongnotchange,longlifenotold.Theirmidstmostgoodissineviltakeoffaltogether,veryhotheartlovetrueGod,loveman.Alllonglonghappy.Firstplace:happyseeJesus''sface,alwaystogetherwithhimlive.Secondly:happyselfnothavesin,evil.Thirdly:happy(because)ancienttimesgoodmen,allangelsatplace:onealtogetherpraisetrueGod.', 'needs_review'),
  ('rcc-100-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 100, 1, NULL, 'To show how glorious heaven is, it is compared to a city with streets of gold, gates of pearl, and walls of jasper and emerald; to a paradise with a river clear as crystal, and the tree of life with healing leaves; to a place of rest after labour: to a father''s house, a happy home.

''They shall obtain joy and gladness, and sorrow and sighing shall flee away. Everlasting joy shall be upon their heads. In his presence is fulness of joy, and at his right hand are pleasures for evermore.'' The best joys of earth are soon gone. Riches fly, health decays, friends depart, death is written on all things.

聖書話天堂地方，好似一個大城市，條條都係金街，城門都係珍珠造嘅，城基又玉石嚟砌嘅。天堂又好似快樂嘅園，又呌做平安嘅地方，又呌做天父嘅屋企。

But the joys of heaven are for ever, and for ever, and for ever. Reader, this heaven may be thine. Jesus keeps the door, but he has opened it wide for all sinners to enter. If you will not come to Jesus, you cannot enter heaven; for he is the door, the only door.

聖書又話，歡喜快活都嚟到嘅，憂愁嘆氣都飛去，永遠嘅快樂戴在頭上，喺眞神面前歡喜到好滿，喺眞神右邊快樂到無窮，本來世上各樣嘅福係假嘅，不過一陣時喺處，錢財噲冇曉，精神都噲失去，朋友都噲離開，世人咁多物件，都噲毀爛嘅。

單係天堂嘅福份，就唔係噉樣，永遠喺處，千萬年不變嘅，而今你想要入天堂，都做得，耶穌係天堂嘅門。有人信佢，耶穌就打開門等你入，你唔肯親就耶穌，就冇別條路入得到，耶穌係路呀，門呀。', 'Toshowhowgloriousheavenis,itiscomparedtoacitywithstreetsofgold,gatesofpearl,andwallsofjasperandemerald;toaparadisewithariverclearascrystal,andthetreeoflifewithhealingleaves;toaplaceofrestafterlabour:toafather''shouse,ahappyhome.''Theyshallobtainjoyandgladness,andsorrowandsighingshallfleeaway.Everlastingjoyshallbeupontheirheads.Inhispresenceisfulnessofjoy,andathisrighthandarepleasuresforevermore.''Thebestjoysofeartharesoongone.Richesfly,healthdecays,friendsdepart,deathiswrittenonallthings.聖書話天堂地方，好似一個大城市，條條都係金街，城門都係珍珠造嘅，城基又玉石嚟砌嘅。天堂又好似快樂嘅園，又呌做平安嘅地方，又呌做天父嘅屋企。Butthejoysofheavenareforever,andforever,andforever.Reader,thisheavenmaybethine.Jesuskeepsthedoor,buthehasopeneditwideforallsinnerstoenter.IfyouwillnotcometoJesus,youcannotenterheaven;forheisthedoor,theonlydoor.聖書又話，歡喜快活都嚟到嘅，憂愁嘆氣都飛去，永遠嘅快樂戴在頭上，喺眞神面前歡喜到好滿，喺眞神右邊快樂到無窮，本來世上各樣嘅福係假嘅，不過一陣時喺處，錢財噲冇曉，精神都噲失去，朋友都噲離開，世人咁多物件，都噲毀爛嘅。單係天堂嘅福份，就唔係噉樣，永遠喺處，千萬年不變嘅，而今你想要入天堂，都做得，耶穌係天堂嘅門。有人信佢，耶穌就打開門等你入，你唔肯親就耶穌，就冇別條路入得到，耶穌係路呀，門呀。', 'needs_review'),
