  ('rcc-103-02', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 103, 2, 'LESSON, XVIII.', 'Ngo-tei²-ke³ Shan tong-yiú³ yan nang shöng-shi pong-cho². Sai siu ke nün² tsai, shi-shi yiú³ lo-mò pong-cho².

Our God ought to-have power always to-help. Tiny little tender children always want (their) mothers to-help.', 'Ngo-tei²-ke³Shantong-yiú³yannangshöng-shipong-cho².Saisiukenün²tsai,shi-shiyiú³lo-mòpong-cho².OurGodoughtto-havepoweralwaysto-help.Tinylittletenderchildrenalwayswant(their)mothersto-help.', 'needs_review'),
  ('rcc-104-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 104, 1, NULL, 'The blind always also need the assistance of their fellow men to lead them; the sick are always in need of the doctor''s help.

We are in this world like little children; like the blind; like the sick: we are like little children—we need some one to protect us; we are like the blind—we need some one to lead us; we are like the sick—we need some one to watch over us. Who has power to help us? Our parents can help us in some matters; in some our teachers and friends; but they can not help us in all things.

盲眼嘅時時亦要人帮助拖佢，有病嘅人時時都要醫生帮助。

我哋喺呢個世界中好似細小嘅嫩仔，好似盲人，好似病人，我哋好似細蚊仔，要一個保佑我哋，好似盲人，要一個拖我哋，好似病人，要一個看守我哋，乜誰有能咁帮助我哋呢，有啲事，父母噲帮助，有啲事，先生朋友噲帮助，但唔係樣樣事噲帮助。

They cannot always be with us. Even if they are beside us, yet they cannot always help us. How can they help us when they are asleep at night? How can they help us if we are far away from them? But we need one who can always help us, so that his mind is always present, his eye never asleep, his arms never weary. Is there such a one? Yes. God who is our Saviour is just such a one.

不能常時同埋我哋，或同埋我哋，亦不能常時帮助，佢到半夜瞓覺，點能帮助我哋呢，或者我哋離開佢好遠，又點能帮助我哋呢，但我哋要一位噲常時帮助，噉就個個心必要時時喺處，眼總唔瞓，手總唔癐，有噉嘅冇呢，有咯，神即係我哋嘅救主，啱啱係噉樣嘅。', 'Theblindalwaysalsoneedtheassistanceoftheirfellowmentoleadthem;thesickarealwaysinneedofthedoctor''shelp.Weareinthisworldlikelittlechildren;liketheblind;likethesick:wearelikelittlechildren—weneedsomeonetoprotectus;weareliketheblind—weneedsomeonetoleadus;wearelikethesick—weneedsomeonetowatchoverus.Whohaspowertohelpus?Ourparentscanhelpusinsomematters;insomeourteachersandfriends;buttheycannothelpusinallthings.盲眼嘅時時亦要人帮助拖佢，有病嘅人時時都要醫生帮助。我哋喺呢個世界中好似細小嘅嫩仔，好似盲人，好似病人，我哋好似細蚊仔，要一個保佑我哋，好似盲人，要一個拖我哋，好似病人，要一個看守我哋，乜誰有能咁帮助我哋呢，有啲事，父母噲帮助，有啲事，先生朋友噲帮助，但唔係樣樣事噲帮助。Theycannotalwaysbewithus.Eveniftheyarebesideus,yettheycannotalwayshelpus.Howcantheyhelpuswhentheyareasleepatnight?Howcantheyhelpusifwearefarawayfromthem?Butweneedonewhocanalwayshelpus,sothathismindisalwayspresent,hiseyeneverasleep,hisarmsneverweary.Istheresuchaone?Yes.GodwhoisourSaviourisjustsuchaone.不能常時同埋我哋，或同埋我哋，亦不能常時帮助，佢到半夜瞓覺，點能帮助我哋呢，或者我哋離開佢好遠，又點能帮助我哋呢，但我哋要一位噲常時帮助，噉就個個心必要時時喺處，眼總唔瞓，手總唔癐，有噉嘅冇呢，有咯，神即係我哋嘅救主，啱啱係噉樣嘅。', 'needs_review'),
