Blind always also want people to-help to-lead them; have sickness people always also want doctor to-help.

We in this [C.] world midst very like tiny small tender children;very like blind men;very like sick people:we very like children-want one [C.] protect us;very like blind men-want one [C.] to-lead us;very like sick men-want one [C.] watch over us. Who has power so to-help us,eh?53. There are some matters father mother can help;some matters teacher (and) friends can help;but not is everykind-of matters can help.

Not able always with us. If with us, also not able always to-help. They arrived midnight sleep sound, how able to-help us, eh? 53. If we are-separated-from them very far, further how help us, eh? 53. But we need one [C.] always to-help, so then that [C.] heart must-needs always at the-place, eye entirely not sleep, hands entirely not tired. Is-there such not, eh? 53. There-is, 32. God just is our Saviour exactly is so fashion.', 'Máng-ngán-keshi-shiyikyiúyanpong-cho²t''o³k''öü;yanpeng²ke³yanshi-shitoyiùyi-shangpong-cho².Ngo-tei²hainikoshaí-kai³chunghòts''zsai''siuke''nün²tsai;hòts''zmángyan;hòts''zpeng²†yan:ngo-tei²hòts''zsai''man-tsai—yiú''yat,ko''pò-yau²ngo-tei²;hòts''zmángyan—yiú''yat,ko''tongo-tei²;hòts''zpeng²†yan—yiú''yat,ko''hon-shaungo-tei².Matshui*yaunangkòmpong-cho²ngo-tei²ni?Yautisz²fú²-mowuipong-cho²;yautisz²sin-shángp''ang-yauwuipong-cho²;tán²mhai²yöng²-yöng²sz²wuipong-cho².Pat,nangshöng-shít''ung-máingo-tei².Wák,t''ung-máingo-tei²,yikpat,nangshöng-shípong-cho².K''öüto''pún''ye²fan''nam,tímnangpong-cho²ngo-tei²ni?Wák,chengo-tei²lei-hoik''öüho''yün,yan²tímpong-cho²ngo-tei²ni?Tán²ngo-tei²yiúyatwai*wuíshöng-shípong-cho²,kòmtsau²koko''sampít,yiú''shi-shihaíshü'',ngántsungmfan,shautsungmkwui².Yaukòmke''mòni?Yaulok.Shantsikhai²ngo-tei²keKau''-chü,ngám-ngamhai²kòmyöng*ke''.Blindalwaysalsowantpeopleto-helpto-leadthem;havesicknesspeoplealwaysalsowantdoctorto-help.Weinthis[C.]worldmidstveryliketinysmalltenderchildren;verylikeblindmen;verylikesickpeople:weverylikechildren-wantone[C.]protectus;verylikeblindmen-wantone[C.]to-leadus;verylikesickmen-wantone[C.]watchoverus.Whohaspowersoto-helpus,eh?53.Therearesomemattersfathermothercanhelp;somemattersteacher(and)friendscanhelp;butnotiseverykind-ofmatterscanhelp.Notablealwayswithus.Ifwithus,alsonotablealwaysto-help.Theyarrivedmidnightsleepsound,howableto-helpus,eh?53.Ifweare-separated-fromthemveryfar,furtherhowhelpus,eh?53.Butweneedone[C.]alwaysto-help,sothenthat[C.]heartmust-needsalwaysatthe-place,eyeentirelynotsleep,h