He wished to-take the-pigs what eat beans husks in-order-to appease (his) hunger : also no man gave things to him to-eat.', '¹Yauyat,ko²yan²yaulöngko³tsai.Ko²sai²tsaitui²fu²-ts''anwa²,''Á²-pá,k''aingoshoyingtak,ke²ku-yip₂fankwo²ngola.''Ko''fú²-ts''antsau²t''unglöngko''tsaifan-hoiká-yip.¹Mò''kéitòyat₂,ko''sai²''tsaitsui²-mai''sho''yauke''ye,höü''hoyünteí²-fongyau-''shá;''haiko''shü''hòfong''tong²,fá-''sán''k''öü-ke''ká-yip.²K''öüyat,titosánts''ingchishí,ko''shu''tei²-fongyautai²kéi-fong;²k''öütsau²mòtakshaí.''Komtsau²höü¹t''au-k''äuko''shü''téi²-fongyatko''yan;ko''yan''ta-fát.k''öühöük''öü-ket''inwai¹chü.¢K''öü''söng¢k''aichü''shoshik₂kc''tau²hok¢laich''ungkeí:to¢mòyan¢péi¢ye¢k''öüshik₂.There-wasa[C.]man(who)hadtwo[C.]sons.Thesmallsontofathersaid,''Father,takeIwhatoughtto-obtainfamilyproperty,dividetome,21.''Thefatherthenfortwo[C.]sonsdividedfamilyproperty.Notverymanydays,theyoungsongatheredtogetherwhateverhadthingswentveryfarplacestrolling;atthatplaceverydissolute(and)squanderedhisfamilyproperty.Heoneatomevendissipatedcompletelytime,thatspot-ofplacehavegreatfamine,hethennotobtain(anything)to-spend.Sothenwent(and)threwhimself(ordependedon)thatspot-ofplaceone[C.]man;themansenthimto-go-tohisfields,tofeedthepigs.Hewishedto-takethe-pigswhateatbeanshusksin-order-toappease(his)hunger:alsonomangavethingstohimto-eat.', 'needs_review'),
  ('rcc-110-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 110, 1, NULL, '<table><tr><td>But when he came to himself he said, ‘How many hired servants of my father’s have bread enough and to spare, and I perish here with hunger! I will arise and go to my father, and will say unto him, “Father, I have sinned against heaven and in thy sight. I am no more worthy to be called thy son; make me as one of thy hired servants.”’</td><td>個陣時佢醒悟起嚟話，我父親咁多工人，佢糧食都有剩，但我喺呢處餓到要死咯。我將起身，去到我父親處，對佢話，亞爸，我得罪天，又得罪你。從今以後，唔敢當做你嘅仔，俾我做你一個工人罷喇。</td></tr><tr><td>And he arose and came to his father. But while he was yet afar off, his father saw him, and was moved with compassion, and ran, and fell on his neck, and kissed him.</td><td>噉就起身，歸到佢父親處。重離好遠，佢父親睇見，就可憐佢，走前去抱住佢頸，共佢親嘴。</td></tr><tr><td>And the son said unto him, ‘Father, I have sinned against heaven, and in thy sight: I am no more worthy to be called thy son.’</td><td>個仔就對佢話，亞爸，我得罪天，又得罪你。從今以後唔敢當叫做你嘅仔咯。</td></tr><tr><td>But the father said to his servants, ‘Bring forth quickly the best robe, and put it on him; and put a ring on his hand, and shoes on his feet: and bring the fatted calf, and kill it, and let us eat, and make merry: for this my son was dead, and is alive again; he was lost, and is found.’ ‘And they began to be merry.’</td><td>佢父親對個啲僕話，即刻攞至好嘅長衫俾佢着，攞戒指戴落佢手指，攞鞋着落佢腳。拉個隻肥牛犢去劏，等我哋快樂嚟食。因爲我呢個仔，死曉又翻生，失曉又得翻嚟。噉就佢哋起首快樂。</td></tr></table>', '<table><tr><td>Butwhenhecametohimselfhesaid,‘Howmanyhiredservantsofmyfather’shavebreadenoughandtospare,andIperishherewithhunger!Iwillariseandgotomyfather,andwillsayuntohim,“Father,Ihavesinnedagainstheavenandinthysight.Iamnomoreworthytobecalledthyson;makemeasoneofthyhiredservants.”’</td><td>個陣時佢醒悟起嚟話，我父親咁多工人，佢糧食都有剩，但我喺呢處餓到要死咯。我將起身，去到我父親處，對佢話，亞爸，我得罪天，又得罪你。從今以後，唔敢當做你嘅仔，俾我做你一個工人罷喇。</td></tr><tr><td>Andhearoseandcametohisfather.Butwhilehewasyetafaroff,hisfathersawhim,andwasmovedwithcompassion,andran,andfellonhisneck,andkissedhim.</td><td>噉就起身，歸到佢父親處。重離好遠，佢父親睇見，就可憐佢，走前去抱住佢頸，共佢親嘴。</td></tr><tr><td>Andthesonsaiduntohim,‘Father,Ihavesinnedagainstheaven,andinthysight:Iamnomoreworthytobecalledthyson.’</td><td>個仔就對佢話，亞爸，我得罪天，又得罪你。從今以後唔敢當叫做你嘅仔咯。</td></tr><tr><td>Butthefathersaidtohisservants,‘Bringforthquicklythebestrobe,andputitonhim;andputaringonhishand,andshoesonhisfeet:andbringthefattedcalf,andkillit,andletuseat,andmakemerry:forthismysonwasdead,andisaliveagain;hewaslost,andisfound.’‘Andtheybegantobemerry.’</td><td>佢父親對個啲僕話，即刻攞至好嘅長衫俾佢着，攞戒指戴落佢手指，攞鞋着落佢腳。拉個隻肥牛犢去劏，等我哋快樂嚟食。因爲我呢個仔，死曉又翻生，失曉又得翻嚟。噉就佢哋起首快樂。</td></tr></table>', 'needs_review'),
