  ('rcc-136-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 136, 1, NULL, '<table><tr><td>friend, am in myself undone by reason of a burden that lieth hard upon me; moreover, I am for certain informed that this our city will be burned with fire from heaven; in which fearful overthrow, both myself, with thee my wife, and you my sweet babes, shall miserably come to ruin; except (the which yet I see not) some way of escape can be found, whereby we may be delivered.'' At this his relations were sore amazed; not for that they believed that what he had said to to them was true, but because they thought that some frenzy distemper had got into his head; therefore, it drawing towards night, and they hoping that sleep might settle his brains, with all haste they got him to bed.</td><td>包袱磧住我，我要敗亡喇，而且我知得實，呢個城，是必被天火所燒，遇着呢個災害之時，我共你哋都要滅亡咯，若唔大早搵定一條生路，點避得角呢，但唔知有噉嘅路冇嗻。妻兒聽聞佢噉講，就好詫異驚慌，唔當佢說話係眞，但估佢係發癲嗻。個時天色將晚，望佢早啲瞓覺，或者定翻佢心，噉就急速催佢去瞓。</td></tr><tr><td>But the night was as troublesome to him as the day; wherefore, instead of sleeping, he spent it in sighs and tears. So, when the morning was come, they would know how he did. He told them, worse and worse: he also set to talking to them again; but</td><td>但佢成晚都好似日頭噉，心中唔安樂，總唔瞓得着，喺處長嗟短嘆，唔歇流眼淚。到天光家人嚟問安，佢話，越耐越見唔安樂，又</td></tr></table>', '<table><tr><td>friend,aminmyselfundonebyreasonofaburdenthatliethharduponme;moreover,Iamforcertaininformedthatthisourcitywillbeburnedwithfirefromheaven;inwhichfearfuloverthrow,bothmyself,withtheemywife,andyoumysweetbabes,shallmiserablycometoruin;except(thewhichyetIseenot)somewayofescapecanbefound,wherebywemaybedelivered.''Atthishisrelationsweresoreamazed;notforthattheybelievedthatwhathehadsaidtotothemwastrue,butbecausetheythoughtthatsomefrenzydistemperhadgotintohishead;therefore,itdrawingtowardsnight,andtheyhopingthatsleepmightsettlehisbrains,withallhastetheygothimtobed.</td><td>包袱磧住我，我要敗亡喇，而且我知得實，呢個城，是必被天火所燒，遇着呢個災害之時，我共你哋都要滅亡咯，若唔大早搵定一條生路，點避得角呢，但唔知有噉嘅路冇嗻。妻兒聽聞佢噉講，就好詫異驚慌，唔當佢說話係眞，