  ('rcc-164-01', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', 'readings-in-cantonese-colloquial', '1894', 164, 1, NULL, 'made Keeper of the Gates, and has commanded him, that with all the Diligence he can, be should look for, search out, and destroy all, and all manner of Diabolonians. And if he lighted upon you, down you go, though your heads were made of gold.'' And now to see how it happened; one of the Lord Willbewill''s faithful soldiers, whose name was Mr. Diligence, stood all this while listening under old Evil-Questioning''s eaves, and heard all the talk that had been betwixt him and the Doubters that he entertained under his roof.

