Further, (it is) said, ''Brothers not agree, (standing-by-the) side people deceive (or oppress) (them).'' If only you (or if you do nothing but pay attention-to) regard your disputes-about trifling tempers; then have men come egg-you-on, (and) stir-up your gossip, or it-is (that they-stir you up) to-fighting, or it-is (that they stir you up) to-law-suits. Entirely there-is-not one [C.] (that) does-not ruin (his) family (property). You, if are filial (and) (feel) affection (and) love (for your relatives), being-of the-people, then you-are good people; being soldiers, then you-are brave-men. But you soldiers (and) people, which one [C.] not know filial piety is (a) good thing; brothers harmonious is good thing? If-already know (it) is good, why further not firm mind, firm strength go do, eh? 53. Must-with heart, continually remember parents (and) brothers. Do-not only do outside ceremonies (or outward forms). Do-not make-light-of (or despise) those little things. Do-not only covet outside persons'' (giving you a) reputation. Do-not (in) former times (be) good, afterwards again not good. So only is truly filial son—', 'ke''shi²-féi;wak₂shi²''tá-tau'',wak₂shi²''tá-kwún-sz.''Tsung''mòyatko''mpai²káke''.''Néi-tei²yökhai²hau-shun²ts''anoi''ni,tsó²man-ke'',chihai²löngman;tsó²pingke'',chihai²''hòhon''.Tán²-hai²néi-tei²pingman,pínyatko''mchi-tohau-shun²hai²''hòsz²;hing-tai²wo-yaphai²''hósz²?Ke''-yínchi-takhai²''hò,tso²-matyau²mshat²sam,shat²likhöütsó²ni?Pit''-söüsam-samním²-ním²kei-chu²fú²-''môhing-tai².M''hòtsing²tsó²ngoi²-min²-ke''yi-man.M''hòfat-lokko''-tisiusz².M''hòtsing²t''amngoi²yan-ke''ming-shing.M''hòts''inshí''hò,hau²-loiyau²m''hò.Komchihai²chan-chan-ke''hau''tsz—chan-chan-ke''hòhing-tai².Néi,yökhai²mhau'',wak₂hai²hing-tai²mwo,tsau²yiu²''k''aiying-fat²ch''ü-chi²lok,tán²''neisamlöümming-pák'',ch''ü-chi²néiyik₂myik.Further,(itis)said,''Brothersnotagree,(standing-by-the)sidepeopledeceive(oroppress)(them).''Ifonlyyou(orifyoudonothingbutpayattention-to)regardyourdisputes